  <para style="h">Dandiel</para>
  <para style="toc1">Dandiel</para>
  <para style="toc2">Dandiel</para>
  <para style="toc3">Dan</para>
  <para style="mt1">Dandiel</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="DAN 1" />
  <para style="s1">Ukpeebñkpọ a-Dandiel Akebọọhọ ke Babilọn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="DAN 1:1" />Ke ayọhọ isua ita ke ini ukara Yehoiyakịm nte adidem ke Yuda, Nebukadnesa adidem Babilọn amaadi Yeruselem anyʌñ adikanna anye akʌk. <verse eid="DAN 1:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="DAN 1:2" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaanyʌñ akappa Yehoiyakịm, adidem Yuda asịn anye ke ubọk, ye ubaak ñkpoduoho tembịd Abasi. Anye amaakoono mme ñkpo ami akaa ke tembịd abasi amọ ke Babilọn<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Hibru ado </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Sina</char></note> anyʌñ akedọñ ke ufọk ubono ñkpọuto abasi amọ.<verse eid="DAN 1:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="DAN 1:3" />Akem adidem amaanọ uyio ate yak Aspenas, adaiwuod ke atu mbon utom ke akwere amọ, asio usʌk nditọ Isrel e-etooho ufọk ubọọñ ye aduuk adidem nọ edinam utom enọ adidem, <verse eid="DAN 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="DAN 1:4" />mfọọn ñkparawa ideen se imiinieghe ndo, enie nti iwuod ukpeep afịd ñkpọ, mme adiọọñọ ñkpọ, esọp iwuod ke unie ifiọk, enyʌñ edot se ikeme edinam utom ke akwere adidem. Anye akenie adikpeep ammọ usem ye ñwed mbʌk mbon Babilọn<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">mbon Kaldi</char></note>. <verse eid="DAN 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="DAN 1:5" />Adidem amaanọ ammọ ubakka ndidia ye ukọd ke usen ke usen a-atooho akpokoro ndidia adidem. Akena enọ ammọ ukpeebñkpọ ke ufañ isua ita, mbemiso eyak ammọ edʌk enam utom ke ufọk adidem.<verse eid="DAN 1:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="DAN 1:6" />Usʌk ke atu mbon se ekesio ekedo mbon Yuda: Dandiel, Hanania, Miseel ye Asaria. <verse eid="DAN 1:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="DAN 1:7" />Ekamba adaiwuod ke atu mbon utom adidem amaanọ ammọ mme ufa anyịñ: Dandiel anye akoot Beltesasa, Hanania anye akoot Sedrak, Miseel anye akoot Mesak; ndin Asaria anye akoot Abedneko.<verse eid="DAN 1:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="DAN 1:8" />Ado Dandiel amaabiide abo ke imọ idiisappake idem imọ ke ndidia ye ukọd ufọk adidem, anye ñko amaabeeñe ekamba adaaha abo ke ayak imọ isappa idem ke utọ usʌñ ami. <verse eid="DAN 1:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="DAN 1:9" />Ndin Abasi amaanam nọ ekamba adaaha awọt Dandiel mfọn mme mbọm, <verse eid="DAN 1:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="DAN 1:10" />ndin adaaha ado amaadọkkọ Dandiel ate, “Ami mmenie ndịk mbaña abọọñ mmi adidem, a-akenịmme ndidia ye ukọd ami inọọ ndufo. Anye adiinam die ikịt naña afo adiọọk idem akan ñkparawa mfen e-edooho ñka isua emana ye afo? Ami ayaanam adidem añwot miin ke ntak iwuod mfo<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Hibru ado </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ndufo</char></note>.”<verse eid="DAN 1:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="DAN 1:11" />Akem Dandiel amaabo awoukpeme a-adaaha ekamba akama utom akesioho abo akpeme Dandiel, Hanania, Miseel ye Asaria ate, <verse eid="DAN 1:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="DAN 1:12" />“Mbọk domo nditọufọk mfo se ke usen duob: Kuunọọ ñnyịn ñkpọ ndomokeed adidia ukan mme ndisi ñkọñ ye unwọnwọñ mmọọñ. <verse eid="DAN 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="DAN 1:13" />Amaanam se idem ñnyịn nyʌñ ben domo ye mme ñkparawa se idia ndidia adidem, ndin nam ye nditọufọk mfo keene se afo akịt.” <verse eid="DAN 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="DAN 1:14" />Anye amaanyịmme anyʌñ adomo ammọ ase ke usen duob.<verse eid="DAN 1:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="DAN 1:15" />Ke utịd usen duob, idem ammọ amaasọñ anyʌñ aseghe akan ake mme ñkparawa e-ekediaha ndidia adidem. <verse eid="DAN 1:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="DAN 1:16" />Ndin awoukpeme ado amaakoono mme nsọñudua ndidia ammọ ye mme ukọd a-akenaaha ammọ enwọñ asio, akappa anọ ammọ ndisi ñkọñ.<verse eid="DAN 1:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="DAN 1:17" />Abasi amaanọ ñkparawa inaañ ami ifiọk ye ikike abaña afịd mbʌk ye ukpeeb. Ñko Dandiel amaanie enọ adidiọọñọ afịd ñkukịd ye ndab.<verse eid="DAN 1:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="DAN 1:18" />Ke utịd ini a-adidem akenịmme abo yak ekoono ammọ esịn ke utom ke akwere amọ, ekamba adaaha amaaben ammọ akaa iso Nebukadnesa. <verse eid="DAN 1:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="DAN 1:19" />Adidem amaaneme nneme ye ammọ, ndin anye ikikịtte mbid Dandiel, Hanania, Miseel ye Asaria ndomokeed; ndin ammọ emaetọọñọ utom ke akwere adidem. <verse eid="DAN 1:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="DAN 1:20" />Ke afịd mme ñkpọ se ibaña aniọñ ye ikike a-adidem akebịppe ammọ, anye amaakịt ke ammọ e-efọn akañ duob ekan afịd mbon unam mmayịk ye mbiaidiọñ ke afịd abioubọọñ amọ.<verse eid="DAN 1:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="DAN 1:21" />Ndin Dandiel amaaba do tutu awuọ akpa isua ukara Adidem Sairọs.<verse eid="DAN 1:21" /></para>
  <chapter eid="DAN 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="DAN 2" />
  <para style="s1">Ndab Nebukadnesa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="DAN 2:1" />Ke ayọhọ isua ukara amọ iba, Nebukadnesa amaadappa mme ndab; akikere amọ amaatịmede, ñko anye ikikanna idaiya idab. <verse eid="DAN 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="DAN 2:2" />Ke ntoro adidem amaanọ uyio ate ekoot mme anam mmayịk, mbiaidiọñ, mbiamfa, mbon ñkukịd ye mme aseutịn yak idọkkọ imọ se ikidappa. Ke ammọ emaekedi edida ke iso adidem, <verse eid="DAN 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="DAN 2:3" />adidem amaabo ammọ ate, “Ami mmedappa ndab amfịnake miin, ndin ñyem adidiọọñọ se anye ada anọ.”<verse eid="DAN 2:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="DAN 2:4" />Ndin mme aseutịn emaebọọrọ adidem ete, “Yak itọñ uwem asọñ adidem! Dọkkọ nditọufọk mfo ndab ado, ndin ñnyịn iyaikappa anye.”<verse eid="DAN 2:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="DAN 2:5" />Adidem amaabọọrọ mme aseutịn ate, “Se ami nsọọñọ mbiere ado ami: adieke ndufo imindọkkọke miin se ñkedappa inyʌñ ikappa anye, ami ñyaanam nọ ikpok ndufo mbai-mbai enyʌñ enam mme ufọk ndufo ekappa eba nte mme eboho mbio. <verse eid="DAN 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="DAN 2:6" />Ado ndufo ekpendọkkọ miin ndab ado enyʌñ esiak se anye awuọ, ami ñyainọ ndufo mme enọ ye mme utịb ye ekamba ukpono. Ke ntoro indọkkọ miin ndab ami inyʌñ ikappa anye innọ.”<verse eid="DAN 2:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="DAN 2:7" />Ammọ emaebọọrọ ini keed mfen ete, “Yak adidem adọkkọ nditọufọk amọ ndab ami, ndin ñnyịn iyaikappa anye.”<verse eid="DAN 2:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="DAN 2:8" />Akem adidem amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, “Ke akpanikọ ami mmesọọñọ ndiọọñọ ke ndufo edep ini, sia ndufo emediọọñọ ke se ami nsọọñọ mbiere ado ami: <verse eid="DAN 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="DAN 2:9" />Adieke ndufo imiitañña ndab ami innọ miin, ufen keed kpọd ana inọọ ndufo. Ndufo emedịbe edioomo edindọkkọ miin abiaña ye mme ndiọi ñkpọ se ikeme edintịn usʌñ, ekere ke ñkpọ ayaakpəho. Do ndin, indọkkọ miin ndab ami, ndin ami ñyaadiọọñọ ke ndufo ekpaekan ekappa anye ennọ miin.”<verse eid="DAN 2:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="DAN 2:10" />Mme aseutịn emaebọọrọ adidem ete, “Ibaaha awo ndomokeed ke ederimbod a-akemeke adinam se adidem abịp abaña ami! Ibaaha adidem ndomokeed, akpọkọm anye akpon die anyʌñ akoñ die, akenaanam a-abịppe utọ ñkpọ ado ato awo unam mmayịk me abiamfa me aseutịn. <verse eid="DAN 2:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="DAN 2:11" />Ñkpọ se adidem abịp asọñ abọhọ. Ibaaha awo ndomokeed a-akemeke adiyaara anye nnọọ adidem ke imiibọhọke mme abasi, ndin ammọ idʌññọ ke atu mbon awo.”<verse eid="DAN 2:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="DAN 2:12" />Ñkpọ ami amaayat anyʌñ afiop adidem esịd eti-eti tutu anye anọ uyio ate ewoot afịd mbon ifiọk ke Babilọn. <verse eid="DAN 2:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="DAN 2:13" />Ndin emaenọ ewʌhọ ebaña adiwot mbon aniọñ, ñko emaenọ mme awo ebo ekeyem Dandiel ye mme ufan amọ nọ ewot ammọ.<verse eid="DAN 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="DAN 2:14" />Ke ini Ariọk, adaiso mbon ukpeme adidem, akewuọhọ aka adiwot mbon ifiọk ke Babilọn, Dandiel amaakama aniọñ ye ikike atañ ikọ ye anye. <verse eid="DAN 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="DAN 2:15" />Anye amaabịp ekamba akama utom adidem ate, “Nsoo ikinam nọ adidem anọ utọ akpọsọñ ewʌhọ ado?” Ndin Ariọk amaanam ñkpọ ami anwaña Dandiel. <verse eid="DAN 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="DAN 2:16" />Akem Dandiel amaadʌk akesoobo ye adidem anyʌñ abeeñe abo yak inọ ini, nọ imọ ikan ikappa ndab ado inọ anye.<verse eid="DAN 2:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="DAN 2:17" />Ndin Dandiel amaanyọñ akaa ufọk amọ anyʌñ akeneme ñkpọ ado anọ mme ufan ammọ Hanania, Miseel ye Asaria. <verse eid="DAN 2:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="DAN 2:18" />Anye amaabo ammọ yak ebeeñe mfọn eto Abasi anyọñ ke abaña ndedịbe ñkpọ ami, mbaak ediwot Dandiel ye mme ufan amọ ukem nte mbon aniọñ mbon ako ke Babilọn. <verse eid="DAN 2:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="DAN 2:19" />Emaeyaara ndedịbe ñkpọ ado ewọt Dandiel ke ñkukịd ke akonayio. Ndin Dandiel amaatooro Abasi anyọñ <verse eid="DAN 2:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="DAN 2:20" />ndin Dandiel amaanyʌñ abo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="DAN 2:20">“Itooro anie anyịñ Abasi ke nsi-nsi nsi-nsi;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="DAN 2:20">aniọñ ye adudu enie anye.<verse eid="DAN 2:20" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="DAN 2:21" />Anye akpəho mme ini ye mme ayio,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="DAN 2:21">anye adooro ndidem anyʌñ adịppe mbon mfen.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="DAN 2:21">Anye anọ mme adiọọñọñkpọ aniọñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="DAN 2:21">anyʌñ anọ mbon ikike ifiọk.<verse eid="DAN 2:21" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="DAN 2:22" />Anye ayaara ntotəño ye ndedịbe ñkpọ;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="DAN 2:22">anye adiọọñọ se isịne ke ekịm,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="DAN 2:22">unwana ñko anyʌñ adʌñ ke anye.<verse eid="DAN 2:22" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="DAN 2:23" />Abasi mme eteete mmi, ami mmukọọm ñnyʌñ utooro fiin:</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="DAN 2:23">Afo amennọ miin aniọñ ye adudu,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="DAN 2:23">afo ameyaara annọ miin se ñnyịn ikubeeñe fiin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="DAN 2:23">afo ameyaara ndab adidem inọ ñnyịn.”<verse eid="DAN 2:23" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Dandiel Akappa Ndab</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="DAN 2:24" />Akem Dandiel amaakaa abịne Ariọk, a-adidem akenịmme abo awot mbon ifiọk ke Babilọn, anyʌñ akedọkkọ anye ate, “Kuuwot mbon aniọñ Babilọn. Mben miin kaa iso adidem, ndin ami ñyaakappa ndab amọ nnọ anye.”<verse eid="DAN 2:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="DAN 2:25" />Ariọk amaaben Dandiel abịne adidem ini keed anyʌñ akebo ate, “Ami mmekịt awo keed ke atu mbon e-ekebenne esio ke abio Yuda a-akemeke aditañ se ndab adidem awuọñọ.”<verse eid="DAN 2:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="DAN 2:26" />Adidem amaabịp Dandiel (e-enyʌññọ ediọọñọ nte Beltesasa) ate, “Nte afo amekeme aditañ se ami ñkekịt ke ndab mmi anyʌñ akappa anye?”<verse eid="DAN 2:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="DAN 2:27" />Dandiel amaabọọrọ, “Ibaaha ata ifiọk ndomokeed, abiamfa, anam mmayịk, me abiaidiọñ a-akemeke adidọkkọ adidem ndedịbe ñkpọ se anye abịp abaña, <verse eid="DAN 2:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="DAN 2:28" />ado a-aba Abasi ke anyọñ a-akemeke adiyaara mme ndedịbe ñkpọ. Anye a-awọt adidem Nebukadnesa se idiitịppe ke mme usen ke ini iso. Ndab mfo ye mme ñkukịd se ikiboiyo ke akikere esịd mfo naña afo akenaaha ke ikʌk mfo edo ami:<verse eid="DAN 2:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="DAN 2:29" />“Naña Afo Adidem akenaaha do, akikere esịd mfo amaawọññọ akaa mme ñkpọ se idiitịppe, ñko andiyaara ndedịbe ñkpọ amauwọt fiin se idiidat itie. <verse eid="DAN 2:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="DAN 2:30" />Ake mmi ado ke, e-eyaara ndịbe ñkpọ ami ennọ miin, idooho nte ami nnie aniọñ se ikpon ikan awo mfen se iba ke uwem, ado nọ Afo Adidem akeme adidiọọñọ ukappa ndab ye se ikisaña iboiyo ke akikere esịd mfo.<verse eid="DAN 2:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="DAN 2:31" />“Afo Adidem amaase, ndin do ke iso mfo ekamba ubobodñkpọ, ataa ekamba, nsem-nsem uyaiya ubobodñkpọ ndise amaada. <verse eid="DAN 2:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="DAN 2:32" />Ekenam iwuod ubobodñkpọ ado ke ataa kold, enam ikpanesịd ye ubọk amọ ke silfa, idịb ye ifʌkkọ amọ ekedo brọns, <verse eid="DAN 2:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="DAN 2:33" />mme ukod amọ ekedo ukwak, ubaak ñkpad amọ ekedo ukwak ndin ubaak ekedo aduañ. <verse eid="DAN 2:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="DAN 2:34" />Idaha a-afo akesʌkkọ ase, emaekpịkke itiad esio, ado idooho ubọk awo akekpịkke. Anye amaatọ ubobodñkpọ ke ukod ukwak ye aduañ amọ anyʌñ asuan ammọ. <verse eid="DAN 2:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="DAN 2:35" />Akema afịd mme ukwak ado, aduañ, brọns, silfa ye kold emaeboomo mbai-mbai enyʌñ ekappa eba nte mbio ke isọñ ukọkñkpọ ke ini ndaayio. Afịm amaakwọọk ammọ asio tutu nduud ibaaha aba. Ado itiad a-aketọọhọ ubobodñkpọ ado amaakappa ekamba abod anyʌñ atọt ayọhọ afịd ederimbod.<verse eid="DAN 2:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="DAN 2:36" />“Ndab ado akedo ami, ndin idahami ñnyịn iyaikappa anye inọ adidem. <verse eid="DAN 2:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="DAN 2:37" />Afo Adidem, afo ado adidem mme ndidem. Abasi anyọñ unọ fiin ukara ye adudu ye ukeme ye ubọọñ; <verse eid="DAN 2:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="DAN 2:38" />anye akappa afịd ubonawo ye mme unam ke ikọd ye mme inuen ke ikpaanyọñ usịn fiin ke ubọk. Nte ammọ ekpedọdʌñ, anye anam afo ado andikara afịd ammọ. Afo ado iwuod kold ado.<verse eid="DAN 2:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="DAN 2:39" />“Afo umaukpọñ ukara, abioubọọñ mfen ayaadakka ada, ado idiikponno nte ake mfo. Akem ayọhọ abioubọọñ ita, ake brọns, ayaada ukara ke afịd ederimbod. <verse eid="DAN 2:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="DAN 2:40" />Ke akpatre, ayọhọ abioubọọñ inaañ ayaaba, asọñ idem nte ukwak, sia ukwak abom anyʌñ anuak afịd ñkpọ, ñko ukem naña ukwak abom ñkpọ mbai-mbai, ukem ado ke anye adiinuak inyʌñ ibom afịd mbon mfen. <verse eid="DAN 2:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="DAN 2:41" />Kpa naña afo akekịt ke ubaak ñkpad ye nnuunukod ekedo aduañ, ubaak ukwak, kpa ntoro abioubọọñ ami ayaanie ubakka; ado anye ayaanie ubaak adudu ukwak ke idem amọ, ukem naña afo akekịt nte ukwak awuaha ye aduañ. <verse eid="DAN 2:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="DAN 2:42" />Kpa naña mme nnuunukod ekedo ubaak ukwak ubaak aduañ, kpa ntoro ke abioubọọñ ami adiido ubaak akpọsọñ ubaak mmeem-mmeem. <verse eid="DAN 2:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="DAN 2:43" />Ñko kpasʌk naña afo akekịt naña ukwak awuaha ye aduañ, kpa ntoro ke mbon ado ediido ñwuaha idiinyʌññọ isọọñọ idiana keed, kpa nte ukwak imiisisọññọ imʌm aduañ ikama.<verse eid="DAN 2:43" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="DAN 2:44" />“Ke ini ukara mme ndidem ado, Abasi anyọñ ayaasio ubọọñ anịm a-awo imiidiisoboke ke nsi-nsi, me ediikpọñ inọ mbon mfen. Anye ayaanuak afịd mme abioubọọñ mbon ñko anyʌñ akịt utịd ammọ, ado anye ke idem amọ ayaasọọñọ ada ke nsi-nsi. <verse eid="DAN 2:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="DAN 2:45" />Ami ado se ñkukịd a-abañake itiad e-ekpịkkeke esio eto ekamba abod ada anọ, ado itooho mme ubọk awo, itiad a-akebuuñọ ukwak, brọns, aduañ, silfa ye kold mbai-mbai.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="DAN 2:45">“Akwa Abasi awọt adidem se idiidat itie ke iniiso. Ndab ami ado akpanikọ ñko adikappa amọ ado se enịm ke akpanikọ.”<verse eid="DAN 2:45" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" sid="DAN 2:46" />Akem Adidem Nebukadnesa amaaduọ ke isọñ ke iso Dandiel anyʌñ akpono anye anyʌñ anọ uyio abo yak enọ anye enọ ye insensi. <verse eid="DAN 2:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="DAN 2:47" />Adidem amaadọkkọ Dandiel ate, “Ke akpanikọ Abasi mfo ado Abasi mme abasi ye <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mme ndidem ye andiyaara mme ndedịbe ñkpọ, sia afo amaakan ayaara ndedịbe ñkpọ ami.”<verse eid="DAN 2:47" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" sid="DAN 2:48" />Ndin adidem amaanịm Dandiel ke ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie anyʌñ anwañña ataa uwak enọ afʌk anye. Anye amaanam Dandiel akara ke afịd ikpeghe ukara Babilọn anyʌñ anam anye adaaha ke atu afịd mbon aniọñ. <verse eid="DAN 2:48" /><verse number="49" style="v" sid="DAN 2:49" />Ke akanna ado, adidem amaakop ebeeñe Dandiel ke adimek Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko nte ikpọ mme adaukara ke ikpeghe ukara Babilọn, ke ini Dandiel ke idem amọ akesʌhọke ke akwere ubọọñ adidem.<verse eid="DAN 2:49" /></para>
  <chapter eid="DAN 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="DAN 3" />
  <para style="s1">Mbid Kold ye Edeme Akwa Ikañ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="DAN 3:1" />Adidem Nebukadnesa amaabot usioidem ake kold, a-akenyọọñọ ke kubid ata anyʌñ anie ukpa kubid itiokeed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho ñkpọ nte ikpad 90 ke ukoñ ye ikpad 9 ke ukpa me ñkpọ nte mita 27 ke ukoñ ye mita 2.7 ke ukpa.</char></note>, anyʌñ asio anye adot ke anwa isọñ Dura ke ikpeghe ukara Babilọn. <verse eid="DAN 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="DAN 3:2" />Anye ndin amaadọñ ekoot mme adaukara ke ikpeghe, mme adaiwuod, mme adaukara, mme anọitem, mme akamaakʌk, mme abiideikpe, mme akpeikpe ye afịd ikpọ mme akama utom ke mme ikpeghe ukara ate edi usọrọ ediben usioidem a-anye akesioho adot. <verse eid="DAN 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="DAN 3:3" />Ke ntoro mme adaukara ke ikpeghe, mme adaiwuod, mme adaukara, mme anọitem, mme akamaakʌk, mme abiideikpe, mme akpeikpe ye afịd ikpọ mme akama utom ke mme ikpeghe ukara emaewuọ edibono ke usọrọ adiben usioidem a-adidem Nebukadnesa akesioho ndot, ndin ammọ emaeda ke iso usioidem ado.<verse eid="DAN 3:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="DAN 3:4" />Asianntọd amaabọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio ate, “Mme idịd ye mme awo ke afịd mme usem, ewʌhọ se inọọ ndufo nọ enịm ado ami: <verse eid="DAN 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="DAN 3:5" />Ndufo emaesʌk ekokop uyio nnʌk, ifiom, ndidoudʌk, ekpa, adʌk ye afịd ndido ñkukwak, ana ndufo eduọ ke isọñ enyʌñ ekpono usioidem kold a-adidem Nebukadnesa asioho anịm. <verse eid="DAN 3:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="DAN 3:6" />Eyaetop awo akeedodo i-imiiduọhọ ke isọñ ikpono usioidem ami esịn ke ataa ekamba ebʌkikañ.”<verse eid="DAN 3:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="DAN 3:7" />Ke ntoro, ammọ ekesʌk ekokop uyio nnʌk, ifiom, ndido udʌk, laiya, ekpa ye afịd ndido ñkukwak, afịd mme idịd ye mme awo ke afịd mme usem emaeduọ ke isọñ enyʌñ ekpono usioidem kold a-adidem Nebukadnesa akebotto adaaha.<verse eid="DAN 3:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="DAN 3:8" />Ke ini ntom usʌk mme aseutịn emaewuọñọ edi enyʌñ ekañ mme Yuu. <verse eid="DAN 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="DAN 3:9" />Ammọ emaedọkkọ Adidem Nebukadnesa ete, “Yak itọñ uwem asọñ adidem ke nsi-nsi! <verse eid="DAN 3:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="DAN 3:10" />Afo Adidem amaanọ ewʌhọ abo awo akeedodo a-akoppo uyom nnʌk, ifiom, ndido udʌk, laiya, ekpa, ye afịd ndido ñkukwak ana aduọ ke isọñ anyʌñ akpono usioidem kold, <verse eid="DAN 3:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="DAN 3:11" />ñko ke eyaetop awo akeedodo i-imiiduọhọ ke isọñ ikpono usioidem ami esịn ke edeme akwa ebʌkikañ. <verse eid="DAN 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="DAN 3:12" />Ado aba ubaak mme Yuu a-afo akenịmme abo ese ñkpọ ebaña ikpeghe ukara Babilọn: Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko, idiikpañña utọñ ikop uyio mfo, Afo Adidem. Ammọ inamma ñkpọ inọ mme abasi mfo, inyʌññọ ikpono usioidem a-afo abotto adaaha.”<verse eid="DAN 3:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="DAN 3:13" />Ke ufiob iyadesịd, Nebukadnesa amaadọñ ekoot Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko. Ndin emaeben ammọ edi ke iso adidem, <verse eid="DAN 3:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="DAN 3:14" />ndin Nebukadnesa amaabịp ammọ ate, “Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko, ado akpanikọ, ke ndufo inamma ñkpọ inọ mme abasi mmi, inyʌññọ ikpono usioidem kold a-ami ñkebotto nnịm? <verse eid="DAN 3:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="DAN 3:15" />Ayaafọn eti-eti, adieke ndufo ebeeñeke idem adiduọ ke isọñ ñnyʌñ ñkpono usioidem a-ami ñkebotto, ndufo emaekop uyio nnʌk, ifiom, ndido udʌk, laiya, ekpa, adʌk ye afịd ñkukwak ikwọ. Ado adieke ndufo imiikponoke anye, eyaitoomo ndufo ini keed edọñ ke edeme ekamba ebʌkikañ. Ndin akee abasi adiikeme adinyaaña ndufo nsio ke ubọk mmi?”<verse eid="DAN 3:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="DAN 3:16" />Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko emaebọọrọ anye ete, “Adidem Nebukadnesa, ufọn ibaaha adifaaña idem ñnyịn ke iso mfo ke abaña ñkpọ ami. <verse eid="DAN 3:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="DAN 3:17" />Adieke itoomoke ñnyịn edọñ ke edeme ekamba ebʌkikañ, Abasi a-ñnyịn inamma ñkpọ inọọ ayainyaaña ñnyịn asio ke edeme ekamba ebʌkikañ, ñko anye ayaifak ñnyịn asio ke ubọk mfo Adidem. <verse eid="DAN 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="DAN 3:18" />Ado akpọkọm anye ifakka ñnyịn, ñnyịn iyem nọ afo adiọọñọ, O! Afo Adidem, ke ñnyịn idiinamma ñkpọ inọ mme abasi mfo, idiinyʌññọ ikpono usioidem kold a-afo abotto adaaha.”<verse eid="DAN 3:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="DAN 3:19" />Ndin esịd Nebukadnesa amaafiop eti-eti ye Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko, ñko ido amọ ke abaña ammọ amaakpəho. Anye amaanọ uyio ate enam ekamba ebʌkikañ afiop akañ itiaba akan naña asido <verse eid="DAN 3:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="DAN 3:20" />anyʌñ anọ ndusʌk mbon ekọñ se ikop adudu ikan ke atu mbon ekọñ amọ uyio ate ebọp Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko enyʌñ etoomo ammọ edọñ ke edeme ekamba ebʌkikañ. <verse eid="DAN 3:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="DAN 3:21" />Emaebọp ammọ, e-ekesịneke ewịra, afọñukod, ekpañ ye mme afọñ mfen, etoomo edọñ ke edeme ekamba ebʌkikañ. <verse eid="DAN 3:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="DAN 3:22" />Sia uyio adidem akedooho ataa usọp-usọp ñko ekamba ebʌkikañ akenekkeke afiop, edemeikañ amaawot mbon ekọñ ekebenne Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko eka ekesịn ke ikañ, <verse eid="DAN 3:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="DAN 3:23" />Ado ideen ita ado, Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko, e-emaekenekke ebọp, emaeduọññọ edọñọ edeme ekamba ebʌkikañ.<verse eid="DAN 3:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="DAN 3:24" />Adidem Nebukadnesa amaabịmme ke ñkpaidem ada ke ukod amọ anyʌñ abịp mme anọitem amọ ate, “Idooho ideen ita ke ñnyịn ikibọp inyʌñ itop isịn ke ikañ?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="DAN 3:24">Ammọ emaebọọrọ, “Ado akpanikọ, Adidem.”<verse eid="DAN 3:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="DAN 3:25" />Anye amaabo ate, “Se, ami mmekịt ideen inaañ naña esaaña ekanna ke esịd ikañ, udʌk ibọppọ ammọ, ñkpọ inyʌññọ inam ammọ, ñko ayọhọ awo inaañ abit ayịn mme abasi.”<verse eid="DAN 3:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="DAN 3:26" />Nebukadnesa ndin amaasaña akpere inua ekamba ebʌkikañ anyʌñ akebọñ akoot, “Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko, nditọufọk Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi, iwuọñọ idi! Idi mi!”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="DAN 3:26">Ndin, Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko emaewuọñọ ke edemeikañ edi, <verse eid="DAN 3:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="DAN 3:27" />ndin mme adaukara ke ikpeghe, mme adaiwuod, mme adaukara, mme anọitem adidem emaewuọñọ edikanna ammọ ekʌk. Ammọ emaekịt ke ikañ ikitaaha ammọ ikpaidem, ikinyʌññọ inyamma ided iwuod ammọ ndomokeed; ikañ ikitaaha afọñidem ammọ, ñko ufịk ikañ ikitebeke ammọ ke idem.<verse eid="DAN 3:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="DAN 3:28" />Nebukadnesa amaabo ate, “Ekọọm anie Abasi Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko, a-akenọọhọ enyere amọ nọ adifak ikọd amọ! Ammọ ekedot anyen ke anye enyʌñ esịn uyio adidem ke mbio enyʌñ enyịmme adiduọọk uwem ammọ utu ke enam ñkpọ enọ me ekpono abasi mfen ke amaaboiyo Abasi ammọ. <verse eid="DAN 3:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="DAN 3:29" />Ke ntoro ami mmenịm ewʌhọ mbo ke eyaekpok mbon awo e-etooho idịd me usem akeedodo mbai-mbai e-etañña idiọọk ebaña Abasi Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko, enyʌñ ekappa ufọk ammọ esịn ke ifịm mbio sia ibaaha abasi mfen a-akemeke adinyaaña ke utọ usʌñ ami.”<verse eid="DAN 3:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="DAN 3:30" />Akem adidem amaabenne Sedrak, Mesak ye Abedneko itie ke ikpeghe ukara Babilọn.<verse eid="DAN 3:30" /></para>
  <chapter eid="DAN 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="DAN 4" />
  <para style="s1">Ndab Nebukadnesa A-abañake Eto</para>
  <para style="pmo">
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">4: </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Ke mme ikpañwed Aramaik ewet Daan 4:1-3 nte Daan 3:31-33, ñko Daan 4:4-37 ewet Daan 4:1-34.</char>
    </note> <verse number="1" style="v" sid="DAN 4:1" />Adidem Nebukadnesa, anọ ekọọm esọk afịd mme abio ye idịd ke afịd mme usem, e-edʌñọke ke afịd iso isọñ: Yak uforo ndufo akpon eti-eti!<verse eid="DAN 4:1" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="DAN 4:2" />Ado inemesịd mmi ami adidọkkọ ndufo mbaña mme utịppe idiọọñọ ye mme utịppeñkpọ ñkpaidem se Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi anam annọọ miin.<verse eid="DAN 4:2" /></para>
  <para style="qm1">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="DAN 4:3" />Mme idiọọñọ amọ ekpon die,</para>
  <para style="qm2" vid="DAN 4:3">Mme akpọsọñ utịppeñkpọ ñkpaidem amọ ekpon die!</para>
  <para style="qm1" vid="DAN 4:3">Abioubọọñ amọ ado nsi-nsi abioubọọñ;</para>
  <para style="qm2" vid="DAN 4:3">ukara amọ asọọñọ ada ke afịd emana.<verse eid="DAN 4:3" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="DAN 4:4" />Ami, Nebukadnesa, ñkeba ke ufọk ke akwere mmi, mmaanie uyʌkkọ ke uwem ye mfọnọñkpọ mmi. <verse eid="DAN 4:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="DAN 4:5" />Ami mmaadappa ndab a-akenamma ami ñkop ndịk. Idaha a-ami ñkesʌkkọ nnaa ke ikʌk, mme ndise ye ñkukịd se ikisaña iboiyo ke akikere esịd mmi emaensịn miin akpọsọñ ndịk ke idem. <verse eid="DAN 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="DAN 4:6" />Ke ntoro ami mmaanọ uyio mbo yak enam afịd mbon aniọñ ke Babilọn edi ke iso mmi edikappa ndab ado ennọ miin. <verse eid="DAN 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="DAN 4:7" />Ami mmaadọkkọ mme anam mmayịk, mbiamfa, mme aseutịn ye mbiaidiọñ ndab ado ke ini ammọ ekedieghe, ado ammọ ikikanna ikappa ndab ado innọ miin. <verse eid="DAN 4:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="DAN 4:8" />Ke akpatre, Dandiel amaadi ke iso mmi, ndin ami mmaadọkkọ anye ndab ado. (Ekoot anye Beltesasa, akeene anyịñ abasi mmi, ndin sịbidịd mme ndisana abasi asịne anye ke idem).<verse eid="DAN 4:8" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="DAN 4:9" />Ami ñkebo, “Beltesasa, etubom mbon unam mmayịk, ami mmediọọñọ ke sịbidịd mme ndisana abasi u-uba fiin ke idem, ndin ibaaha ndedịbe ñkpọ a-asọññọ ukan fiin adiyaara. Se ndab mmi mi: Kappa anye nnọ miin. <verse eid="DAN 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="DAN 4:10" />Mme ñkukịd se ami ñkekịt idaha a-ami ñkenaaha ke ikʌk edo ami: Ami mmaase, ndin se eto adaaha mi ke iso mmi ke ufọọd isọñ. Anye amaanekke anyọọñ. <verse eid="DAN 4:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="DAN 4:11" />Eto ado amaakọt, akpon anyʌñ anyọọñ aketuuk ikpaanyọñ; emaeda ke afịd utịd ederimbod ekịt anye. <verse eid="DAN 4:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="DAN 4:12" />Mme mfañ amọ emaefọọn, mfịd amọ ewak, anye akenyʌñ ado ndidia anọ afịd awo. Mme unam ikọd emaenie itie nduọkadudu ke idak amọ, mme inuen emaenyʌñ edʌñ ke mme ñkọk amọ, afịd ñkpọ se ebobot emaenie ndidia eto anye.<verse eid="DAN 4:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="DAN 4:13" />“Ke mme ñkukịd a-ami ñkekịtte ke ini nnaaha ke ikʌk, ami mmaase, ndin se keed a-akedooho adisana amaanda miin ke iso, isʌñutom<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4:13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme ido </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">awoukpeme</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; se ñko ke Daan 4:17 ye 23.</char></note>, a-atooho hefịn asọiyọ adi. <verse eid="DAN 4:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="DAN 4:14" />Anye amaatañ ke akpọsọñ uyio ate: ‘Kpịkke eto ado nyʌñ kpooño mme ñkọk amọ sịññe, kịp mme mfañ amọ nyʌñ suan mfịd amọ, yak mme unam efeeñe ewuọñọ ke idak amọ, mme inuen enyʌñ esọọrọ ke mme ñkọk amọ. <verse eid="DAN 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="DAN 4:15" />Ado yaak itak ye mme adʌñ amọ, e-ebọppọ ke ukwak ye brọns, esʌk esịne ke isọñ, ke mbid inwañ.</para>
  <para style="pm" vid="DAN 4:15">“ ‘Yak mbara hefịn afʌk anye, ñko yak anye anyʌñ adʌñ ye mme unam ke ufọọd mme eto ke iso isọñ. <verse eid="DAN 4:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="DAN 4:16" />Yak ekpəho akikere esịd amọ esio ekpọñ awo enyʌñ ekappa enọ anye akikere unam, tutu isua itiaba aboiyo.<verse eid="DAN 4:16" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="DAN 4:17" />“ ‘Mme isʌñutom eben etob ami edi, mme ndisana awo esian ubiere ami, nọ mme aduuwem ediọọñọ ebo ke Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi akaara ke afịd mme abioubọọñ ke iso isọñ anyʌñ ayaak ammọ anọ awo akeedodo a-anye amaaha anyʌñ anịm nsuuhoñkan awo nte adaaha ke iwuod ammọ.’<verse eid="DAN 4:17" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="DAN 4:18" />“Ndab se ami, Adidem Nebukadnesa, ñkedappa ado ami. Ke ntoro, Beltesasa, ndọkkọ miin se ado awuọñọ, sia ibaaha awo aniọñ ndomokeed ke abioubọọñ mmi akanna akappa anye annọọ. Ado afo amekeme, sia sịbidịd mme ndisana abasi usịne fiin ke idem.”<verse eid="DAN 4:18" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Dandiel Akappa Ndab</para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="DAN 4:19" />Ndin idem amaakpa Dandiel (e-ekenyʌññọ ekoot Beltesasa) ke etək ini; akikere amọ amaasịn anye ndịk ke idem. Ke ntoro adidem amaabo anye ate, “Beltesasa, kuuyak ndab ado me se anye ada anọ atịmede esịd mfo.”</para>
  <para style="pm" vid="DAN 4:19">Beltesasa amaabọọrọ anye ate, “Abọọñ mmi, akpekapado ndab ami abaña mme asua mfo ñko se anye ada anọ akpebaña mbon utọk mfo! <verse eid="DAN 4:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="DAN 4:20" />Eto a-afo akekịtte, a-akekọttọ atara anyʌñ asọñ idem, e-etịñe amọ aketuuho ikpaanyọñ, nọ ekịt ke afịd iso isọñ, <verse eid="DAN 4:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="DAN 4:21" />ye mfọọn mfañ ye uwak mfịd, a-akenọọhọ afịd awo ndidia, anọ mme unam ikọd itie nduọkadudu, anyʌñ anie mme itie efọk ke ñkọk amọ anọ mme inuen, <verse eid="DAN 4:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="DAN 4:22" />Adidem Mmi, afo ado eto ado! Afo amekpon anyʌñ asọñ adudu, ubom mfo atara tutu awuọ ikpaanyọñ, ñko ukara mfo atara akewuọ mme ñnyan itie ke ekondo.<verse eid="DAN 4:22" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="DAN 4:23" />“Afo Adidem amaakịt adisana awo keed, isʌñutom, nte asọiyọ ato hefịn adi adibo, ‘Kpịkke eto ami nyʌñ sobo anye, ado saana itak amọ yaak, e-ebọppọ ke ukwak ye brọns, ke mbid inwañ, ke ini mme adʌñ amọ esʌhọke ke isọñ. Yak mbara a-atooho anyọñ afʌk anye, yak anye adʌñ ye mme unam ikọd, tutu isua itiaba aboiyo.’<verse eid="DAN 4:23" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="DAN 4:24" />“Adidem Mmi, se ndab ado awuọ ado ami, ñko ami ado ewʌhọ a-Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi anọọhọ abọọñ mmi adidem: <verse eid="DAN 4:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="DAN 4:25" />Eyaubịne fiin esio ke atu mbon awo ndin afo ayaadʌñ ye mme unam ikọd; afo ayaata mbid nte abaakenañ ndin mbara ayaanyʌñ ato hefịn ufʌk fiin. Isua itiaba ayaubọhọ fiin tutu afo awọt ke iminyịmme ibo ke Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi ada ukara ke afịd abioubọọñ ke iso isọñ anyʌñ ayaak ammọ anọ awo akeedodo a-anye amaaha. <verse eid="DAN 4:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="DAN 4:26" />Ubiere adisaana itak eto ado ye mme adʌñ ñyaak awuọñọ ke eyaemaana ekappa ubọọñ mfo unọ fiin ke ini afo amaawọt unyịmme ke Hefịn akara. <verse eid="DAN 4:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="DAN 4:27" />Ke ntoro, Afo Adidem, yak unem fiin esịd adikop item mmi: kañ mme ndiọiñkpọ mfo ke adinam se inen, ye ibak mfo ke adifọn ido ye mbon se efiik. Akeme adido ke uforo mfo ayaakaa iso ke afo amaanam ami.”<verse eid="DAN 4:27" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ndab ado Awuọ Asu</para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="DAN 4:28" />Afịd ñkpọ ami amaatịppe anọ Adidem Nebukadnesa. <verse eid="DAN 4:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="DAN 4:29" />Ke afiọñ duob mme iba amaakeboiyo, nte adidem akesʌkkọ asaña ke anyọñ ufọk ke akwere ubọọñ Babilọn, <verse eid="DAN 4:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="DAN 4:30" />anye amaabo ate, “Nte ami idooho akwa Babilọn a-ami ñkebọppọ, nte itie idʌñ ubọọñ, ke akpọsọñ adudu mmi nnọ itooro ubọọñ mmi?”<verse eid="DAN 4:30" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="DAN 4:31" />Idaha a-anye akesʌkkọ atatañ ikọ ado ke inua, uyio amaato ke hefịn abo anye ate, “Ewʌhọ u-unọọhọ fiin ado ami, Adidem Nebukadnesa: U-ubọ fiin adudu ubọọñ mfo. <verse eid="DAN 4:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="DAN 4:32" />Eyaubịne fiin esio ke atu mme awo, afo ñko ayaadʌñ ye mme unam ikọd; afo uduuta mbid nte abaakenañ. Isua itiaba ayauboiyo fiin tutu afo awọt unyịmme ke Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi ada ukara ke afịd mme abioubọọñ ke iso isọñ anyʌñ ayaak ammọ anọ awo akeedodo anye ayemme.”<verse eid="DAN 4:32" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="DAN 4:33" />Ataa idaha ado se eketañ ebaña Nebukadnesa amaawuọ asu. Emaebịne anye esio ke atu mme awo, ndin anye amaanyʌñ ata mbid nte abaakenañ. Mbara anyọñ amaafʌk anye idem tutu ided akọt anye ke idem nte ñwa ntrukpuum, mbara amọ anyʌñ adunyọñ nte mbara inuen.<verse eid="DAN 4:33" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="DAN 4:34" />Ke ini ado amaakeboiyo, ami Nebukadnesa, mmaadịppe anyen mmi nse anyọñ, ndin mmaamaana ndiọọñọ idem. Do ndin ami mmaakọọm Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi; ami mmaakpono ñnyʌñ ntooro anye a-aduuho uwem ke nsi-nsi.</para>
  <para style="qm1" vid="DAN 4:34">Ukara amọ ado nsi-nsi ukara;</para>
  <para style="qm2" vid="DAN 4:34">ubọọñ amọ asọọñọ ada ke afịd emana.<verse eid="DAN 4:34" /></para>
  <para style="qm1">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="DAN 4:35" />Ebat afịd mme awo ke iso isọñ</para>
  <para style="qm2" vid="DAN 4:35">ke ikpu-ikpu.</para>
  <para style="qm1" vid="DAN 4:35">Anye anam se anye ama</para>
  <para style="qm2" vid="DAN 4:35">ye mme adudu anyọñ</para>
  <para style="qm2" vid="DAN 4:35">ye mme awo ke iso isọñ.</para>
  <para style="qm1" vid="DAN 4:35">Awo ndomokeed ikemeke adimʌm anye ubọk ñkama</para>
  <para style="qm2" vid="DAN 4:35">me adibịp anye mbo, “Nsoo ke afo anam?”<verse eid="DAN 4:35" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="DAN 4:36" />Kpa ke ukem ini a-ami ñkemaanake ndiọọñọ idem, emaemaana eyaak ukpono ye uku mmi ennọ miin ke ntak itooro abioubọọñ mmi. Mme anọitem ye mme ikpọ mbon ukara mmi emaedʌk eñyem miin, ndin emaemaana emben miin edot ke ebekpo mmi ndin mmaanie ukpono ñkan naña ñkenie akpa. <verse eid="DAN 4:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="DAN 4:37" />Idahami, ami Nebukadnesa, mmetooro ñnyʌñ ndịppe anyịñ ñnyʌñ nnọ Adidem anyọñ ubọọñ, sia afịd ñkpọ se anye anam ado eti ñko afịd mme usʌñ amọ edo ndinen. Ndin anye akeme adisuuhọ afịd mbon se isaña ke ntañidem.<verse eid="DAN 4:37" /></para>
  <chapter eid="DAN 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="DAN 5" />
  <para style="s1">Ubọkñwed ke Ndibene</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="DAN 5:1" />Adidem Belsasa amaanam ekamba usọrọ ndidia ndubiayio anọ ikpọ mbon ukara amọ, awo tọsịn keed (1,000), anyʌñ anwọñ ukọd ye ammọ. <verse eid="DAN 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="DAN 5:2" />Naña Belsasa akesʌkkọ anwọñ ukọd amọ, anye amaanọ uyio ate ekekoono mme ukpok kold ye silfa e-ete amọ Nebukadnesa akekoonoke ato tembịd ke Yeruselem adi, nọ adidem ye mme ñkpisọñ amọ, ibaan ndọ ye ibaan esa amọ ekama enwọñ ñkpọ. <verse eid="DAN 5:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="DAN 5:3" />Akem ammọ emaekoono mme ukpok kold e-eketañña esio ke tembịd Abasi ke Yeruselem, ndin adidem ye mme ñkpisọñ, ibaan ndọ ye ibaan esa amọ emaekama ammọ enwọñ ñkpọ. <verse eid="DAN 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="DAN 5:4" />Nte ammọ ekesʌkọ enwọñ ukọd, ammọ emaetooro mme abasi e-ebotto ke kold ye silfa, brọns, ukwak, eto ye itiad.<verse eid="DAN 5:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="DAN 5:5" />Ke unana idodanyen mme nnuunubọk awo emaewuọ ewet ñkpọ ke ndibene a-akekpereke ñkpọ udodikañ ke akwere ubọọñ adidem. Adidem amaase naña ubọk ado awet ñkpọ. <verse eid="DAN 5:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="DAN 5:6" />Iso amaabọkkọ adidem, ñko ndịk amaanam anye tutu ukod amọ ameem ndin edọñ amọ edutọọrọ.<verse eid="DAN 5:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="DAN 5:7" />Adidem amaadọñ ekoot mbiaidiọñ, mme aseutịn ye mbiamfa. Ndin anye amaadọkkọ mbon aniọñ ami ke Babilọn ate, “Awo akeedodo akanna akoot ubọkñwed ami anyʌñ andọkkọ miin se anye ada anọ, eyaesịn anye iduod-iduod afọñ enyʌñ ekọọñ anye kold ke itọñ, ñko eyaenam anye ado ayọhọ adaukara ita se ikoñ ikan ke Babilọn.”<verse eid="DAN 5:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="DAN 5:8" />Ndin afịd mbon aniọñ adidem emaedʌk edi, ado ammọ ikikanna ikoot me adikappa ubọkñwed ado. <verse eid="DAN 5:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="DAN 5:9" />Ke ntoro idem amaadọdiọñ anyeñ adidem Belsasa ndin iso anyʌñ adọdiọñ abọkkọ anye. Idem amaakpa mme ñkpisọñ amọ.<verse eid="DAN 5:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="DAN 5:10" />Abọọñanwaan amaadʌk adi afe ndidia, ke ini anye akekoppo uyio adidem ye ake mme ñkpisọñ amọ. Anye amaabo, “Yak itọñ uwem asọñ adidem ke nsi-nsi! Kuukop ndịk! Kuunyʌñ uba ke mfʌhọ! <verse eid="DAN 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="DAN 5:11" />Aba awo ke abioubọọñ mfo a-anieghe sịbidịd mme ndisana abasi ke idem. Ke ini ukara ete mfo, ekekịt anye nte awo a-anieghe ikike ye ifiọk ye aniọñ ukem nte mme abasi. Ete mfo, Adidem Nebukadnesa, akemek anye nte abọọñ ke atu mbon unam mmayịk, mbiaidiọñ, mme aseutịn ye mbiamfa. <verse eid="DAN 5:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="DAN 5:12" />Anye akenam ami sia Dandiel, a-adidem akekoodo Beltesasa, amaanie eti iwuod, ifiọk ye ndiọọñọ idem, anyʌñ anie ukeme adikappa ndab, adisiak ñke, ñnyʌñ ñyọọ ñkpọsọñ mfịna. Dọñ ekoot Dandiel, ndin anye ayaudọkkọ fiin se ubọkñwed ado awuọñọ.”<verse eid="DAN 5:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="DAN 5:13" />Ke ntoro emaeben Dandiel edi iso adidem, ndin adidem amaabịp anye abo, “Nte afo ado Dandiel, keed ke atu mbon ekebịneke esio ke abio e-ete mmi adidem akebenne ato Yuda adi? <verse eid="DAN 5:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="DAN 5:14" />Ami mmekop ke sịbidịd mme abasi aba ye afo, ñko ke afo amenie ntotəño ifiọk, ikike ye ñwuọnda aniọñ. <verse eid="DAN 5:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="DAN 5:15" />Emaeben mbon aniọñ ye mbiaidiọñ edi ke iso mmi adikoot ubọkñwed ami ñnyʌñ indọkkọ miin se anye awuọ, ado ammọ ikikanna ikappa. <verse eid="DAN 5:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="DAN 5:16" />Idahami ami mmekop ke afo amekeme adikappa anyʌñ ayọ mme ñkpọsọñ mfịna. Adieke afo akanna akoot ubọkñwed ami anyʌñ andọkkọ miin se anye awuọñọ, eyausịn fiin iduod-iduod afọñ enyʌñ ukọọñ fiin ñkpọitọñ kold, ñko eyaunam fiin ado ayọhọ awo ita se ikoñ ikan ke ukara abioubọọñ ami.”<verse eid="DAN 5:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="DAN 5:17" />Akem Dandiel amaabọọrọ adidem ate, “Afo amekeme adinịm mme enọ mfo nnọọ idem mfo anyʌñ anọ awo mfen utịb mfo. Ado ikpanna ami adikoot ubọkñwed ami nnọ adidem ñnyʌñ ndọkkọ anye se awuọñọ.<verse eid="DAN 5:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="DAN 5:18" />“Afo Adidem, Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi amaanọ ete mfo Nebukadnesa ukara ye ubom ye ubọọñ ye uyai. <verse eid="DAN 5:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="DAN 5:19" />Ke ntak ñkoñ-ñkoñ itie A-Abasi akenọọhọ anye, afịd mme idịd ye mme awo ye mme usem emaebaak enyʌñ ekpono anye. Mbon se adidem akeyem adiwot, anye amaawot; mbon se anye akeyem inịm uwem, anye amaasaana ayaak; anye amaabenne mbon se anye akeyem adidịppe itie; ñko mbon se anye akeyem isuuhọ itie, anye amaasuuhọ. <verse eid="DAN 5:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="DAN 5:20" />Ado ke ini ñkokkoidem ye isọñesịd ye ntañidem ekedʌkkọ esịd amọ, emaedooro anye ke ebekpo ubọọñ amọ enyʌñ ebọ anye ubọọñ amọ. <verse eid="DAN 5:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="DAN 5:21" />Emaebịne anye esio ke atu mme awo enyʌñ enọ anye esịd unam; anye akedʌñ ye mme dọñki ikọd anyʌñ ata mbid nte abaakenañ, mbara amaato ke anyọñ afʌk anye idem, tutu anye akenyịmme abo ke Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi ado andikara ke afịd abioubọọñ ke iso isọñ anyʌñ anọ awo a-anye ayemme akara ammọ.<verse eid="DAN 5:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="DAN 5:22" />“Ado afo, Belsasa, ayịn amọ, usuuhọke idem mfo, akpesʌkado afo amaadiọọñọ afịd ami. <verse eid="DAN 5:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="DAN 5:23" />Utu ke ado, afo amedịppe idem mfo ke anyọñ anyʌñ adomo idem mfo ye <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> hefịn. Afo amaanam nọ esịññe mme ukpok ke tembịd amọ usọk fiin, ñko afo ye ñkpisọñ mfo, ibaan ndọ ye ibaan esa mfo emaekama ammọ enwọñ ukọd. Afo amaatooro mme abasi ake silfa ye kold, brọns, ukwak, eto ye itiad, idiikanna ikịt ñkpọ me ikop ñkpọ me idiọọñọ ñkpọ. Ado afo ukukponoke Abasi a-akamake uwem mfo ye afịd usʌñ mfo ke ubọk amọ. <verse eid="DAN 5:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="DAN 5:24" />Do ndin anye amaanọ ubọk akewette ñkpọ ado.<verse eid="DAN 5:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="DAN 5:25" />“Ñkpọ e-ekewette ado ami:</para>
  <para style="pc" vid="DAN 5:25">
    <char style="sc">Mene, Mene, Tekel, Parsin</char><verse eid="DAN 5:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="DAN 5:26" />“Se mme ikọ ami ewuọñọ edo ami:</para>
  <para style="p" vid="DAN 5:26">“<char style="tl">Mene</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5:26 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Mene </char><char style="ft" closed="false">akeme ido </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">adibat </char><char style="ft" closed="false">me </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">mina </char><char style="ft" closed="false">(udomo akʌk).</char></note>: Abasi abat mme usen ukara mfo, anyʌñ aben anye akesịm utịd.<verse eid="DAN 5:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="DAN 5:27" />“<char style="tl">Tekel</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5:27 </char><char style="fq" closed="false"><char style="tl">Tekel</char> </char><char style="ft" closed="false">akeme iwuọñọ </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">edidomo </char><char style="ft" closed="false">me </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">sekel.</char></note>: Emauben fiin edot ke udomo ñkpọ, ndin ekịt ebo ke afo uyọhọke.<verse eid="DAN 5:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="DAN 5:28" />“<char style="tl">Peres</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5:28 </char><char style="fq" closed="false"><char style="tl">Peres</char> </char><char style="ft" closed="false">akeme iwuọñọ </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">adibakka </char><char style="ft" closed="false">me </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Pesia </char><char style="ft" closed="false">me </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ubaak mina </char><char style="ft" closed="false">me </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ubaak sekel.</char></note>: E-ebakka abioubọọñ mfo enyʌñ eyaak enọ mbon Miid ye mbon Pesia.”<verse eid="DAN 5:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="DAN 5:29" />Ndin Belsasa amaanọ uyio ate, esịn Dandiel iduod-iduod afọñ, ekọọñ anye ñkpọitọñ kold, enyʌñ esian anwa-anwa ke anye ado ayọhọ ñkponñkan atu adaukara ita ke abio Babilọn.<verse eid="DAN 5:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="DAN 5:30" />Emaewot Belsasa, adidem Babilọn, kpa ke akonayio ado, <verse eid="DAN 5:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="DAN 5:31" />ndin Dariọs awo Miid amaadat ubọọñ, anye akedo awo isua ata mme iba.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5:31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke ikpañwed Aramaik ufañ ami Daan 5:31 ewet Daan 6:1.</char></note><verse eid="DAN 5:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="DAN 5" />
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="DAN 6" />
  <para style="s1">Dandiel ke Ube mme Ekpe</para>
  <para style="p">
    <note caller="+" style="f">
      <char style="fr" closed="false">6: </char>
      <char style="ft" closed="false">Ke ikpañwed Aramaik Daan 6:1-28 ewet Daan 6:2-29.</char>
    </note> <verse number="1" style="v" sid="DAN 6:1" />Akedo ñkpọ inemesịd Dariọs adimek mme iwuod ikpeghe ukara ikie mme edịb (120) adikara ke afịd abioubọọñ, <verse eid="DAN 6:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="DAN 6:2" />ye mme adaiwuod ukara ita, a-akeed ke atu ammọ akedooho Dandiel. Mme iwuod ikpeghe ukara ekeba ke idak mme adaiwuod ukara nọ ato do ukaara adidem asaña afọn. <verse eid="DAN 6:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="DAN 6:3" />Dandiel amaanekke anam utom amọ awuọ ada asaña-asaña ke atu mme iwuod ikpeghe ukara ye mme adaiwuod ukara ato eti ubọkutom amọ tutu adidem aduak adisio anye nnịm nte akwa adaiwuod ke afịd abioubọọñ amọ. <verse eid="DAN 6:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="DAN 6:4" />Ke ntak ado, mme adaiwuod ukara ye mme iwuod ikpeghe ukara emaeyem usʌñ adidot Dandiel ikọ ke abaña naña anye anam utom ukara, ado ammọ ikikanna ikịt idiọọk ke utom amọ. Ammọ ikikịtte ñwo ke idem amọ, sia anye amaanam akpanikọ, idiaha ñwo inyʌññọ ikpọt ke utom amọ. <verse eid="DAN 6:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="DAN 6:5" />Ke akpatre ideen ado emaebo ete, “Ñnyịn idiikịtte ntak se idot Dandiel uyio ibọhọke ñkpọ se ibaña mbed Abasi amọ.”<verse eid="DAN 6:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="DAN 6:6" />Ndin mme adaiwuod ukara ye mme iwuod ikpeghe ukara emaekaa nte atu awo keed ebịne adidem ekebo anye ete: “Yak itọñ uwem asọñ Adidem Dariọs ke nsi-nsi! <verse eid="DAN 6:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="DAN 6:7" />O! Adidem, afịd mme ikpọawo ukara, mme adaaha, iwuod ikpeghe ukara, mme anọitem ye mme adaukara enyịmme ebo ke akpena adidem anọ mbed anyʌñ asọọñọ ewʌhọ ami abo ke awo ndomokeed a-abọññọ akam anọ abasi akeedodo me awo ke ufañ usen edịb mme duob ke iso, ibọhọke ado afo, ke eyaetop anye esịn ke ube mme ekpe. <verse eid="DAN 6:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="DAN 6:8" />O! Adidem, nam ewʌhọ ami nyʌñ nam ewet ke ñwed mbaak edikan ekpəho anye, akeene mbed mbon Miid ye Pesia, a-awo imiikemeke adikpəho.” <verse eid="DAN 6:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="DAN 6:9" />Do ndin Adidem Dariọs amaawet ewʌhọ ado asịn ke ñwed.<verse eid="DAN 6:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="DAN 6:10" />Ndin ke ini Dandiel amaakediọọñọ ke emaesuan etob ewʌhọ ami, anye amaanyọñ ufọk ke ubeed ufọkanyọñ amọ ke itie u-ubenafịm anaaha inwañ ase Yeruselem. Anye amaatọọñọ edọñ abọñ akam akañ ita ke usen anọ Abasi amọ ekọọm, ukem naña anye akesidak anam. <verse eid="DAN 6:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="DAN 6:11" />Akem ideen ado emaesaña nte atu ekekịt nte Dandiel abọñ akam anyʌñ abeeñe Abasi unwam. <verse eid="DAN 6:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="DAN 6:12" />Ndin ammọ emaekaa ke iso adidem ekeneme ye anye ke abaña ewʌhọ adidem ete: “O! Adidem. Nte afo ukuwette ewʌhọ anwa-anwa ubo ke awo akeedodo a-abọññọ akam anọ abasi me awo ndomokeed ke imiibọhọke afo, ke usen edịb mme duob ke iso, ke eyaetop anye esịn ke ube mme ekpe?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="DAN 6:12">Adidem amaabọọrọ ate, “Ewʌhọ ado mmọdo ada, asaña akeene mbed mbon Miid ye Pesia, a-awo imiikemeke adikpəho.”<verse eid="DAN 6:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="DAN 6:13" />Do ndin ke ammọ ekedọkkọ adidem ete, “O! Adidem, Dandiel, a-adooho keed ke atu mbon se ekekoono esio ke abio Yuda, ikpañña utọñ ikop se afo atañ, me ewʌhọ afo awette ke ñwed. Anye asʌk abọbọñ akam akañ ita ke usen anọ Abasi amọ.” <verse eid="DAN 6:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="DAN 6:14" />Akikere amaatịmede adidem eti-eti, ke anye adikikop ikọ ami; anye amaanekke abiide adifak Dandiel nsio, tutu ayio usen ado akekịm, adidem amaanyʌñ adomo afịd ukeme adinyaaña anye.<verse eid="DAN 6:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="DAN 6:15" />Akem mme ideen ado emaesaña ke atu ekaa iso Adidem Dariọs enyʌñ ekebo anye ete, “Adidem Ñnyịn, toiyo bo ke naña asịne ke mbed mbon Miid ye Pesia awo ikemeke adikpəho ewʌhọ me mbed adidem awuukọ.”<verse eid="DAN 6:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="DAN 6:16" />Do ndin adidem amaanọ uyio, ammọ ñko emaeben Dandiel edi enyʌñ etop anye esịn ke ube mme ekpe. Adidem amaadọkkọ Dandiel abo, “Yak Abasi mfo, a-afo anamma ñkpọ anọọ afịd ini, ufak fiin asio!”<verse eid="DAN 6:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="DAN 6:17" />Emaeben itiad efʌk ke inua ube ado, ndin adidem amaakọp anye anyʌñ akama ñkpannuun amọ ye ake mme ñkpisọñ amọ afiik idiọọñọ anịm, mbaak edikpuho se ekebiere ebaña Dandiel. <verse eid="DAN 6:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="DAN 6:18" />Ndin adidem amaanyọñ esa abọọñ amọ, ado anye ikidiaha ndidia, inyʌññọ iyak mbon mbre edi iso amọ afịd akonayio ado. Ñko anye ikikanna idaiya idab.<verse eid="DAN 6:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="DAN 6:19" />Ke ataa akpa utịn usiere, adidem amaasọp idem adakka akaa ube mme ekpe ado. <verse eid="DAN 6:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="DAN 6:20" />Anye akesaña akpere ube ado, anye amaabọñ akoot Dandiel ke uyio mfʌhọ, “Dandiel, awo Abasi uwem, nte Abasi mfo, a-afo anamma ñkpọ anọọ afịd ini akan ufak fiin asio ke atu mme ekpe?”<verse eid="DAN 6:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="DAN 6:21" />Dandiel amaabọọrọ ate, “Yak itọñ uwem asọñ adidem ke nsi-nsi! <verse eid="DAN 6:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="DAN 6:22" />Abasi mmi amaadọñ mme enyere amọ, ñko anye amaakuup mme ekpe inua. Ammọ innamma miin idiọọk, sia anye ikikịtte ndudue mmi ke iso amọ. Akenaanam ami ñko nnamma idiọọk ke iso mfo, O! Adidem.”<verse eid="DAN 6:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="DAN 6:23" />Adidem amaayọhọ ye inemesịd, anye amaanyʌñ anọ uyio ate edịppe Dandiel esio ke ube. Ndin emaedịppe Dandiel esio ke ube, awo ikikịtte unan ndomokeed ke idem amọ, sia anye amaabuọt idem ke Abasi amọ.<verse eid="DAN 6:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="DAN 6:24" />Ke uyio adidem, emaeben ibon e-ekedotto Dandiel uyio eketop edọñ ke ube mme ekpe ukem ye mme ibaan ye nditọ ammọ. Mme ekpe ado emaekan ammọ ubọk, enyʌñ eboom akpọ ammọ mbemiso ammọ ekewuọwuọ esịd isọñ ube ado.<verse eid="DAN 6:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="DAN 6:25" />Ndin Adidem Dariọs amaawet anọ afịd mme idịd ye mme awo ke afịd usem ke iso isọñ ate:</para>
  <para style="pmo" vid="DAN 6:25">“Yak uforo ndufo awak!<verse eid="DAN 6:25" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="DAN 6:26" />“Ami mmenọ ewʌhọ mbo ana nte mme awo ke afịd idaha abioubọọñ mmi ebaak enyʌñ ekpono Abasi Dandiel.</para>
  <para style="qm1" vid="DAN 6:26">“Sia anye ado aduuwem Abasi,</para>
  <para style="qm2" vid="DAN 6:26">ñko anye aba ke nsi-nsi;</para>
  <para style="qm1" vid="DAN 6:26">abioubọọñ amọ idiibiarake,</para>
  <para style="qm2" vid="DAN 6:26">ukara amọ idiinieghe utịd.<verse eid="DAN 6:26" /></para>
  <para style="qm1">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="DAN 6:27" />Anye a-afak anyʌñ anyaaña;</para>
  <para style="qm2" vid="DAN 6:27">anye a-anam mme idiọọñọ ye utịppeñkpọ</para>
  <para style="qm2" vid="DAN 6:27">ke mme hefịn ye ke isọñ.</para>
  <para style="qm1" vid="DAN 6:27">Anye amaafak Dandiel</para>
  <para style="qm2" vid="DAN 6:27">asio ke adudu mme ekpe.”<verse eid="DAN 6:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="DAN 6:28" />Ndin ñkpọ amaafọn ye Dandiel ke ini ukara Dariọs ye ke ini ukara Sairọs awo Pesia.<verse eid="DAN 6:28" /></para>
  <chapter eid="DAN 6" />
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="DAN 7" />
  <para style="s1">Dandiel Adappa Ndab abaña Amọn Inaañ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="DAN 7:1" />Ke akpa isua ukara Belsasa, adidem Babilọn, Dandiel amaadappa ndab, mme ñkukịd ñko emaenyʌñ eboiyo anye ke akikere ke ini anye akenaaha ke ikʌk. Anye amaawet akpan ñkpọ se ibaña ndab ado.<verse eid="DAN 7:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="DAN 7:2" />Dandiel amaabo ate, “Ke ñkukịd mmi ke akonayio ami mmaase, ndin ke iso mmi ami mmaakịt afịm anyọñ mbeñ inaañ nte ebịmme ewuọ ebəkko akwa akpainyañ. <verse eid="DAN 7:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="DAN 7:3" />Ikpọ amọn inaañ, ammiidubiottoke emọ-emọ ndomokeed, emaeto ke inyañ ewuọñọ edi.<verse eid="DAN 7:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="DAN 7:4" />“Akpa akeba nte ekpe, anyʌñ anie mba nte ntrukpuum. Ami mmaase tutu ediwai mme ñwa amọ esịññe enyʌñ edịppe anye ekpọñ isọñ, ndin anye amaada ke ukod iba nte awo, ñko emaenam anye akere ñkpọ nte ataa awo.<verse eid="DAN 7:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="DAN 7:5" />“Ñko ayọhọ amọn iba amaaba ke iso mmi, a-akebaaha nte amọn. Emaedịppe anye ke ñkañ amọ keed, ñko anye akefịbe mme akpọñkañ ita ke inua ke ufọọd eded amọ. Ndin emaebo ate, ‘Dakka da nyʌñ ta abʌkunam nọ uyʌkkọ!’<verse eid="DAN 7:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="DAN 7:6" />“Ke ado amaakeboiyo, ami ñkese, ayọhọ amọn ita amaada ke iso mmi, anye akebit ekpeikọd. Ñko anye akenie mba inaañ ke edem amọ nte inuen. Amọn anye ami akenie iwuod inaañ, ndin emaenọ anye unen adikara.<verse eid="DAN 7:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="DAN 7:7" />“Ke ado amaakeboiyo, ami mmaakịt ke ñkukịd mmi ke akonayio, ayọhọ amọn inaañ mmọ ke iso mmi akeda, anie ndịk ye akwa adudu. Anye akenie ikpọ eded ukwak; ndin anye amaanuak anyʌñ ata afịd se anye akekịt anyʌñ asọnnọ se ikisʌhọ ke idak ñkpad. Anye amaanie adiañña ye afịd mme amọn mbon ako, anye akenie nnʌk duob.<verse eid="DAN 7:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="DAN 7:8" />“Ami ñkesʌk ñkere mbaña mme nnʌk ado, se nnʌk mfen mi ke iso mmi, etək nnʌk, a-akewuọhọ ato atu ammọ; ndin emaekpʌkkọ nnʌk ita ke iso atu mme akpa nnʌk ado. Nnʌk ami akenie anyen nte anyen awo anyʌñ akpoon inua ikọ.<verse eid="DAN 7:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="DAN 7:9" />“Naña ami ñkesʌkkọ nse,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="DAN 7:9">“emaenam mme ebekpo ewuọñọ eda ke mme itie,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="DAN 7:9">ñko Abasi Usen Esed amaatie ke itie amọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="DAN 7:9">Afọñidem amọ akesana nte sino;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="DAN 7:9">ided iwuod amọ akesana nte mfịdukịm.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="DAN 7:9">Ebekpo amọ akesak ye edemeikañ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="DAN 7:9">mme wiil amọ afịd ekedo ikañ-ikañ.<verse eid="DAN 7:9" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="DAN 7:10" />Ikañ amaasakka nte inyañ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="DAN 7:10">awuọ ato iso amọ adi.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="DAN 7:10">Tọsịn ke tọsịn ekese ñkpọ ebaña anye;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="DAN 7:10">tọsịn duob ke tọsịn duob ekeda ke iso amọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="DAN 7:10">Esob emaebono,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="DAN 7:10">emaenyʌñ ekʌppọ mme ñwed.<verse eid="DAN 7:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="DAN 7:11" />“Ndin ami mmaakaa iso nse ato ke ntak ñkpoon inua ikọ a-nnʌk ado aketañña. Ami mmaakaa iso nse tutu ewot amọn ado enyʌñ esobo ikpọkidem amọ enyʌñ etop esịn ke ekamba edemeikañ ado. <verse eid="DAN 7:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="DAN 7:12" />(Emaebọi mme amọn mbon ako adudu ammọ, ado emaeyaak ammọ edu uwem ke etok ini).<verse eid="DAN 7:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="DAN 7:13" />“Ke ñkukịd mmi ke akonayio ami mmaase, ndin se ke iso mmi anye a-akebitte ayịn awo, naña adi ye ntọñanyọñ ke hefịn. Anye amaasaña akpere Abasi Usen Esed ndin emaeben anye ekaa iso amọ. <verse eid="DAN 7:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="DAN 7:14" />Emaenọ anye adudu, ukpono ye unen adida ke idem ñkara; afịd mme idịd ye mbon awo ke afịd mme usem emaekpono anye. Ubọọñ amọ ado nsi-nsi ubọọñ i-idiiduakka iboiyo mfep, ñko abioubọọñ amọ ado anye se awo idiiduakka ibiat ke nsi-nsi.<verse eid="DAN 7:14" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adikappa Ndab ado</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="DAN 7:15" />“Ami, Dandiel mmaanie mfʌhọ ke sịbidịd, ñko mme ñkukịd se ikiboiyo ke akikere esịd mmi emaentịmede miin. <verse eid="DAN 7:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="DAN 7:16" />Ami mmaasaña ñkpere keed ke atu mbon se ikida do ñnyʌñ mbịp anye se afịd ami awuọọñọ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="DAN 7:16">“Ndin anye amandọkkọ anyʌñ annọ miin uyaara afịd mme ñkpọ ami: <verse eid="DAN 7:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="DAN 7:17" />‘Mme ikpọ amọn inaañ ami edo ndidem inaañ se idiito ke ederimbod iwuọ ida. <verse eid="DAN 7:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="DAN 7:18" />Ado mme ndisana ikọd Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi eyaebọ ubọọñ enie ke nsi-nsi, ado ntoro, ke nsi-nsi nsi-nsi.’<verse eid="DAN 7:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="DAN 7:19" />“Ndin ami mmaayem adidiọọñọ se ayọhọ amọn inaañ ada anọ, a-akenieghe ukpʌhọde ye afịd mbon ako, a-akenyʌññọ anekke anie ndịk, ye eded ukwak amọ ye mbara brọns; amọn a-akenuakka anyʌñ ata mbon se anye akekan anyʌñ asọọk se ikisʌhọ ke ñkpad. <verse eid="DAN 7:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="DAN 7:20" />Ami ñko mmaayem adidiọọñọ mbaña mme nnʌk duob ke iwuod amọn ye nnʌk keed anye ako a-akewuọhọ ada, ake ita mbio ako ekeduọññọke ke iso amọ, nnʌk anye akekoñño akan mbio ako, a-akenyʌññọ anie anyen ye inua, a-aketañña ikọ ye ñkpoon inua. <verse eid="DAN 7:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="DAN 7:21" />Ami ñkese, nnʌk ami akesʌk anwana ekọñ ye mme ndisana awo anyʌñ akan ammọ, <verse eid="DAN 7:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="DAN 7:22" />tutu Abasi Usen Esed adi adinọ ubiideikpe nọ atoppo ndisana ikọd Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi, ndin ini amaadikem a-ammọ ekedidatta abioubọọñ enie.<verse eid="DAN 7:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="DAN 7:23" />“Anye amaanọ uyaara ami: ‘Ayọhọ amọn inaañ ami ado ayọhọ abioubọọñ se idiiba ke ederimbod. Anye ayaakpʌhọ ye afịd mme abioubọọñ mbon ñko, ayaanyʌñ aben afịd ederimbod amen, asọọk anye ke isọñ anyʌñ anuak anye. <verse eid="DAN 7:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="DAN 7:24" />Mme nnʌk duob ado edo mme ndidem duob se idiito iwuọñọ ke abioubọọñ ami. Ammọ emaesọiyọ, adidem mfen ayaawuọ ada ukara, anie adiañña ye mbon usen edem; anye ayaasịn mme ndidem ita ke idak amọ. <verse eid="DAN 7:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="DAN 7:25" />Anye ayaatañ ikọ adian Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi anyʌñ afiik ndisana ikọd Abasi anyʌñ anwana adikpuuñọ mme ini ye mme mbed. Eyaekappa ndisana awo edọñ ke ubọk amọ ke ini keed, mme ini ye ubaak ini.<verse eid="DAN 7:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="DAN 7:26" />“ ‘Ado esob eyaebono ikpe, ndin eyaebọ anye adudu enyʌñ esobo anye afịd-afịd ke nsi-nsi. <verse eid="DAN 7:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="DAN 7:27" />Ndin eyaekappa ubọọñ, adudu ye ubom afịd mme abioubọọñ ke anyọñ enọ ndisana ikọd Ñkoñ Ñkan Abasi. Abioubọọñ amọ adiido nsi-nsi abioubọọñ, ñko afịd mme adaukara eyaekpono enyʌñ ekop uyio amọ.’<verse eid="DAN 7:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="DAN 7:28" />“Utịd ñkukịd ado ami. Ami, Dandiel mmaanekke nnie mfʌhọ ke akikere mmi, ndin iso amambọkkọ, ado ami mmaasịn ñkpọ ami ke esịd mmi.”<verse eid="DAN 7:28" /></para>
  <chapter eid="DAN 7" />
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="DAN 8" />
  <para style="s1">Ñkukịd Dandiel a-Abañake Akukịmedọñ ye Ebod</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="DAN 8:1" />Ami, Dandiel mmaakịt ñkukịd ke ayọhọ isua ita ke ini ukara Adidem Belsasa, ke anye a-ami ñketooho ñkịt amaakeboiyo. <verse eid="DAN 8:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="DAN 8:2" />Ke ñkukịd mmi ami mmaakịt idem mmi ke esịd akpọsọñ itie ke Susa ke ikpeghe Elam; ke ñkukịd ado ami ñkeba ke ñkañ Akpaubom Ulai. <verse eid="DAN 8:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="DAN 8:3" />Ami ñkebenne anyen nse, se akukịmedọñ ye nnʌk iba ke iso mmi, ada ke ñkañ akpaubom ado, mme nnʌk ado emaedunyọñ. Keed ke atu mme nnʌk iba ado amaanyọọñ akan keed, ado amaadikọt ke akpatre. <verse eid="DAN 8:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="DAN 8:4" />Ami mmaakịt nte akukịmedọñ ado abịmme adʌk aka usobutịn, adoro ye usuuk. Ibaaha unam ndomokeed a-akekanna akpan anye, ñko inyʌññọ iba se ikikan ifak nsio ke adudu amọ. Anye akenam se inem anye ke idem anyʌñ akaa iso akpon.<verse eid="DAN 8:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="DAN 8:5" />Nte ami ñkesʌkkọ ñkere mbaña ñkpọ ami, ebod amaawuọ ke ataa iyokko ato usobutịn adi ye ñwuọnda nnʌk ke iso ufọọd anyen amọ, afrọ aboiyo ke afịd ederimbod, ado ukod amọ ikituuho isọñ. <verse eid="DAN 8:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="DAN 8:6" />Anye amaasaña akpere akukịmedọñ a-akenieghe nnʌk iba a-ami ñkekịtte nte ada ke ñkañ akpaubom anyʌñ abịmme abịne anye ke akpọsọñ ifiobesịd. <verse eid="DAN 8:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="DAN 8:7" />Ami mmaakịt naña anye anwana ye akukịmedọñ ado ke ifiobesịd, atuak anye anyʌñ abʌñ nnʌk amọ naña iba. Akukịmedọñ ado ikinieghe adudu adida anye ke iso; ebod ado amaatuak anye atọ ke isọñ anyʌñ asọnnọ anye ke ukod, ndin ikibaaha se ikan ifak akukịmedọñ ado isio ke adudu amọ. <verse eid="DAN 8:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="DAN 8:8" />Ebod ado amaanekke anie adudu, ado ke ataa ekamba adudu amọ, ekamba nnʌk ado amaabʌññọ awuọ, ndin ke itie amọ mme awuọiso nnʌk inaañ emaetịppe ewuọ esak iso ese iso mbañ inaañ afịm e-etooho anyọñ.<verse eid="DAN 8:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="DAN 8:9" />Nnʌk mfen amaatịppe ato keed ke atu ammọ, a-aketọọñọke etək-etək ado akọt ke adudu, atara akewuọ usuuk ye usakkautịn tutu ukañ Uyaiya Isọñ. <verse eid="DAN 8:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="DAN 8:10" />Anye amaakọt tutu akesịm mme udịm hefịn, anye amaanyʌñ atop ubaak udịm ntantaafiọñ aduọọk ke isọñ anyʌñ afiik ammọ ke ñkpad. <verse eid="DAN 8:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="DAN 8:11" />Anye amaabenne idem amọ tutu akpon nte adaiso udịmekọñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>; anye amaaben uwa afịd usen <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> afep, anyʌñ awuut adisana itie idʌñ amọ. <verse eid="DAN 8:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="DAN 8:12" />Ato ke ntak nsọñiwuod, emaeyaak ikọd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ye uwa afịd usen enọ anye. Anye amaaforo ke afịd ñkpọ se anye akenam, ndin emaetop akpanikọ eduọọk ke isọñ.<verse eid="DAN 8:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="DAN 8:13" />Akem ami mmaakop naña adisana awo atañ ikọ, ndin adisana awo mfen amaabo anye ate, “Adiikpeene die mbemiso ñkukịd ami awuọ asu, ñkukịd a-abañake uwa afịd usen, nsọñiwuod a-adatta ñwuudo adi, adiyaak adisana itie idʌñ nnọọ ye adisọnnọ udịm ikọd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ke idak ñkpad?”<verse eid="DAN 8:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="DAN 8:14" />Anye amandọkkọ miin ate, “Adiidat ndubiayio ye ubakusen tọsịn iba mme ikie ita; ndin eyaemaana enam adisana itie asana.”<verse eid="DAN 8:14" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adikappa Ñkukịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="DAN 8:15" />Ke ini ami Dandiel, ñkeseeghe ñkukịd ado nsʌk ñnwana adidiọọñọ se anye awuọñọ, anye a-akebitte awo amaada ke iso mmi. <verse eid="DAN 8:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="DAN 8:16" />Ndin ami mmaakop uyio awo nte akoot ato Ulai, “Kebreel, dọkkọ awo ami se ñkukịd ami awuọñọ.”<verse eid="DAN 8:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="DAN 8:17" />Idaha a-anye akesañake akpere itie a-ami ñkedaaha, idem amañnyeñ miin, ami mmaanyʌñ nduọ ñnyanna nnaa ke isọñ. Anye amambo miin, “Ayịn awo, diọọñọ bo ke ñkukịd ami abaña utịd ini.”<verse eid="DAN 8:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="DAN 8:18" />Idaha a-anye akesʌkkọ atañ ikọ annọ miin, ami ñkeba ke ataa akpọsọñ idab, iso mmi amaanyʌñ akʌbọ ke isọñ. Ndin anye amantuuk miin anyʌñ andịppe miin adaaha ke ñkpad mmi.<verse eid="DAN 8:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="DAN 8:19" />Anye amaabo ate, “Ami mbuudọkkọ fiin se idiitịppe ke ukpereedem ini ifiobesịd, sia ñkukịd ami abaña ini enịmme enọ anye ke utịd ini. <verse eid="DAN 8:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="DAN 8:20" />Akukịmedọñ a-afo akekịtte nte anie nnʌk iba ada anọ ndidem Media ye Pesia. <verse eid="DAN 8:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="DAN 8:21" />Adusu ebod ado ada anọ adidem Kriis, ndin ekamba nnʌk ke ufọọd anyen amọ ada anọ akpa adidem. <verse eid="DAN 8:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="DAN 8:22" />Mme nnʌk inaañ e-edatta itie a-anye akebʌññọke aduọ ada anọ mme abioubọọñ inaañ se idiito idịd amọ iwuọ, ado idiinieghe ukem adudu nte anye.<verse eid="DAN 8:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="DAN 8:23" />“Ke ukpereedem ini ukara ammọ, ke ini mbon nsọñiwuod emaenekke enam ibak, aniendịk adidem, ataa ayọhọ awo a-adiọọñọke ñkara, ayaada ukara. <verse eid="DAN 8:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="DAN 8:24" />Anye ayaanie akpọsọñ adudu, ado idiitooho adudu idem amọ. Anye ayaabiat ñkpọ tutu idem akpa afịd awo anyʌñ akịt unen ke se adodo anye anamma. Anye ayaasobo mme ñkpọsọñ ye mme ndisana awo. <verse eid="DAN 8:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="DAN 8:25" />Anye ayaaforo ato abiaña anyʌñ akịt idem amọ nte mfiọkñkan. Ke ammọ emaekere ke imisọọñọ ida, anye ayaasobo akpakʌb awo anyʌñ anwana ye Akpan ke atu mme akpanabọọñ. Kpayeado eyaesobo anye, ado idiitooho adudu ubọk awo.<verse eid="DAN 8:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="DAN 8:26" />“Ñkukịd ake mme ndubiayio ye mme ubakusen e-ekunọọhọ fiin ado akpanikọ, ado fʌk ñkukịd ado nịm, sia anye abaña anyan ini ke iso.”<verse eid="DAN 8:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="DAN 8:27" />Ami, Dandiel mmaakop ekaha ke idem. Ami mmaanaa ke mmemidem ke uwak usen. Akema ami mmaadakka nda ñkenam utom adidem. Ñkukịd ado amaanam mbọribọ antuak miin; anye amambọ ifiọk.<verse eid="DAN 8:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="DAN 8" />
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="DAN 9" />
  <para style="s1">Akam Dandiel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="DAN 9:1" />Ke akpa isua ukara Dariọs ayịn Seeses<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke Hibru ado </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Ahasuerus</char></note> (awo ubon Media), e-ekenamma nọ ado adaukara ke abio Babilọn; <verse eid="DAN 9:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="DAN 9:2" />ke akpa isua ke ini ukara amọ, ami, Dandiel mmaadiọọñọ nto Ñwed Abasi, akeene ikọ se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> akenọọ prọfed Yerimaiya, abo ke ñwuudo Yeruselem adiido isua ata mme duob. <verse eid="DAN 9:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="DAN 9:3" />Ndin ami mmaawọññọ iso nse <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ñnyʌñ ñkpe anye ubọk ke akam ye ebeeñe, ke utreudia, ye ke usịne afọñikpo ye ke ntọñ.<verse eid="DAN 9:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="DAN 9:4" />Ami mmaabọñ akam nnọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi mmi ñnyʌñ ñyaara idiọọkñkpọ mmi:</para>
  <para style="pm" vid="DAN 9:4">“<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> mmi, akwa ye anie ndịk Abasi, a-anịmme enwọñọ ima amọ ye mbon se ima anye inyʌñ inịm mme ewʌhọ amọ, <verse eid="DAN 9:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="DAN 9:5" />ñnyịn iminam idiọọkñkpọ inyʌñ udue fiin. Ñnyịn imibak ibak inyʌñ isọñ iwuod; ñnyịn imiwuọ ikpọñ mme ewʌhọ mfo ye mme mbed mfo. <verse eid="DAN 9:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="DAN 9:6" />Ñnyịn ikpañña utọñ inọ mme isʌñutom mfo mme prọfed, e-eketañña ikọ ke anyịñ mfo enọ ndidem ñnyịn, nditọ ideen abọọñ ye mme eteete ñnyịn, ye afịd mbon awo ke abio.<verse eid="DAN 9:6" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="DAN 9:7" />“<char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, afo ado adinen, ado mfịn ami abuud ifʌk ñnyịn iso; mbon Yuda ye mbon se idʌñọ ke Yeruselem ye afịd Isrel, ke ñkped-ñkped ye ke nsan-nsan, ke afịd mme abio se afo isuan ñnyịn adọñ ke ntak unana mbuọdidem ñnyịn ke afo. <verse eid="DAN 9:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="DAN 9:8" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, abuud i-ifʌk ñnyịn iso ye ndidem ñnyịn, nditọ ideen abọọñ ye mme eteete ñnyịn, sia ñnyịn imudue fiin. <verse eid="DAN 9:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="DAN 9:9" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ñnyịn anie mbọm ye ndakkannọ, akpesʌkado ñnyịn imaisọñ iwuod ye anye; <verse eid="DAN 9:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="DAN 9:10" />ñnyịn ikoppo uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ñnyịn, inyʌññọ inịm mme mbed se anye akinọọ ñnyịn ato mme isʌñutom amọ mme prọfed. <verse eid="DAN 9:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="DAN 9:11" />Afịd Isrel e-ebiat mbed mfo enyʌñ ewọññọ ekpọñ usʌñ, ke adisịn adikop uyio mfo.</para>
  <para style="pm" vid="DAN 9:11">“Ke ntoro e-enwañña mme isuuñọ ye mme ubiere enwọñọ se ekewet ke Mbed Moses, awo Abasi, ifʌk ñnyịn ke idem, sia ñnyịn imudue fiin. <verse eid="DAN 9:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="DAN 9:12" />Afo amenam mme ikọ se eketañ ibaña ñnyịn ye mme adaukara ñnyịn ewuọ esu ke adiben ekamba nnananyen inọọ ñnyịn. Akenam awo inamma utọ ñkpọ e-enamma Yeruselem mi akpa ke afịd idak anyọñ. <verse eid="DAN 9:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="DAN 9:13" />Kpa naña ewet ke Mbed Moses, afịd ukuud ami isịm ñnyịn, kpayeado, ñnyịn inieghe aniọñ iyem mfọn <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ñnyịn, ke adikappa esịd ñkpọñ mme idiọọkñkpọ ñnyịn ñnyʌñ ñkpañ utọñ nnọọ akpanikọ mfo. <verse eid="DAN 9:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="DAN 9:14" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ikibiatta ini adiben ukuud ami idot ñnyịn, sia <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ñnyịn anen ke afịd se anye anam, ado ñnyịn ikoppo uyio amọ.<verse eid="DAN 9:14" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="DAN 9:15" />“Idahami, <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ñnyịn, a-akebenne ikọd mfo asio ke isọñ Iyib ye akwa ubọk, a-akenyʌññọ anam anyịñ mfo awuọ etob tutu usen mfịn ami, ñnyịn imudue fiin, iminam idiọọkñkpọ. <verse eid="DAN 9:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="DAN 9:16" /><char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, nte asañake ke mme ndinen adinam mfo, wọññọ iyadesịd ye ikpakkaesịd mfo kpọñ Yeruselem, abio mfo, adisana abod mfo. Ndiọiñkpọ ñnyịn ye mme ukwaññkpọ mme eteete ñnyịn e-enam Yeruselem ye ikọd mfo edo ñkpọ nsaha enọ afịd mbon se ikanna ñnyịn ikʌk.<verse eid="DAN 9:16" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="DAN 9:17" />“Mbọk, Abasi ñnyịn, kop mme akam ye ebeeñe awo mfo idahami. Ke ntak mfo, mbọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, nie mbọm baña ñwuudo adisana itie idʌñ mfo. <verse eid="DAN 9:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="DAN 9:18" />Abasi ñnyịn, mbọk kpañ utọñ nyʌñ kop; tat anyen mfo nyʌñ se ñwuudo abio a-akereke Anyịñ mfo. Ñnyịn inamma mme ebeeñe ami unọ fiin ato ke adinenido ñnyịn, ado ato ke ntak akwa mbọm mfo. <verse eid="DAN 9:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="DAN 9:19" />Abọọñ! Mbọk kpañ utọñ! Abọọñ, mbọk feen! Abọọñ, mbọk kop nyʌñ nam! Ke ntak mfo, Abasi mmi, mbọk kuukpeene, sia abio mfo ye mbon mfo ekere Anyịñ mfo.”<verse eid="DAN 9:19" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Ata mme Duob i-itie Itiaba</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="DAN 9:20" />Ke idaha a-ami ñkesʌkkọ ntañ ikọ ñnyʌñ mbọñ akam, ñyaara ndudue mmi ye ndudue ikọd mmi Isrel, ñnyʌñ nnam ebeeñe mmi nnọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi mmi ke ntak adisana abod amọ; <verse eid="DAN 9:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="DAN 9:21" />ke ini ami ñkesʌkkọ mba ke akam, Kebreel, awo a-ami ñkekịtte ke akaan ñkukịd, amaasọp afeghe ambịne ke idaha ini uwa ndubiayio. <verse eid="DAN 9:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="DAN 9:22" />Anye amannọ item anyʌñ ambo miin ate, “Dandiel, ami mmedi idahami adunọọ fiin ikike ye ifiọk. <verse eid="DAN 9:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="DAN 9:23" />Kpa idaha a-afo aketọọñọke adibọñ akam, uyio amaawuọ, a-anamma nọ ami ndi ndudọkkọ fiin, sia afo amenekke anie ukpono. Ke ntoro, tịm kere ikọ ado nyʌñ diọọñọ ñkukịd ado:<verse eid="DAN 9:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="DAN 9:24" />“Ata mme duob ke itie itiaba ado ini enịmme enọ ikọd mfo ye adisana abio mfo adibiat mbed mmaa, aditre unam idiọọkñkpọ, adikpe ubọk ke ibak, adiben nsi-nsi adinenido ndʌk ndi, aditre ñkukịd ye prọfesi ye adinyʌñ ñyet Ataa Adisana Itie adan nnịm.<verse eid="DAN 9:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="DAN 9:25" />“Diọọñọ nyʌñ nie ifiọk baña ami: Tọọñọ ke ini se ikọ akewuọ yak emaana ediọñ enyʌñ etịmme ebọp Yeruselem tutu a-anye e-Ekeyette Adan Enịm, andikara, adi, adiido itiaba ‘ke itiaba,’ ata mme iba ke ‘itiaba.’ Eyaemaana ebọp anye ye mme efaak ye ukpe, ado adiido kpa ke ini ukuud. <verse eid="DAN 9:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="DAN 9:26" />Ke mme ata mme iba ke ‘itiaba’ ado emaeboiyo, eyaewot Anye e-Ekeyette Adan Enịm ñko anye idiinieghe ñkpọ ndomokeed. Mbon andikara ado se idiidi eyaebiat abio ye adisana itie. Utịd ini adiidi nte mmọọñ ukwọ: Ekọñ ayaakaa iso tutu utịd, emaenyʌñ ewet mme nsobo enịm. <verse eid="DAN 9:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="DAN 9:27" />Ndin anye ayaasọọñọ edioomo ye uwak awo ke ufañ udua keed. Ñko ke ufọọd udua ado anye ayaatre uwa ye enọ. Ndin anye a-anamma nsobo ayaato ke mba mme mbubiam adi, tutu enwañña utịd e-ewette enọ anye efʌk anye.”<verse eid="DAN 9:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="DAN 9" />
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="DAN 10" />
  <para style="s1">Ñkukịd Dandiel a-abañake Awo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="DAN 10:1" />Ke ayọhọ isua ita ke ukara Sairọs, adidem Pesia, emaenọ Dandiel (e-ekekoodo Beltesasa) uyaara. Etob a-Dandiel akebọọhọ ato uyaara ado akedo akpanikọ, ñko anye akebaña ekamba ekọñ. Ekeyaara ifiọk etob ado enọ anye ke ñkukịd.<verse eid="DAN 10:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="DAN 10:2" />Ke ini ado, ami Dandiel, mmaafʌhọ udua ita. <verse eid="DAN 10:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="DAN 10:3" />Ami ñkidiaha umemek ndidia, unam me ukọd ndomokeed ikinyʌññọ ituuk ñkpọkinua mmi; ñko ami ñkifiọññọke adan ndomokeed tutu mme udua ita ado eboiyo.<verse eid="DAN 10:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="DAN 10:4" />Idaha ami ñkedaaha ke mben akwa inyañ Tikris, ke ayọhọ usen edịb mme inaañ ke akpa afiọñ, <verse eid="DAN 10:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="DAN 10:5" />ami ñkebenne anyen nse, awo a-akesịneke linen afọñ mmọdo ada ke iso mmi, atobo uyaiya ñkpaha isịn kold a-atooho Ufas akanna isịn amọ. <verse eid="DAN 10:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="DAN 10:6" />Idem amọ akeba nte topas, iso aba nte akebkeb, anyen aba nte edemeikañ, ubọk ye ukod nte unwana atọọtʌk brọns, ndin uyio amọ akeba nte uyom atu awo.<verse eid="DAN 10:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="DAN 10:7" />Ami, Dandiel ñkedo ukweeñe awo a-akekịtte ñkukịd ado; mbon se ikiba ye ami ikikịtte anye, ado utọ akwa uteeñe se ikimʌm ammọ amaanam ammọ efeeñe ekedịbe. <verse eid="DAN 10:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="DAN 10:8" />Ke ntoro ami ikpọọñ ñkese ekamba ñkukịd ado; adudu ikimbaaha miin aba ke idem, iso amambiara unam ndin unwam ikibaaha innọ miin. <verse eid="DAN 10:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="DAN 10:9" />Ami mmaakop naña anye atañ ikọ, ndin nte ami ñkekpañña utọñ nnọ anye, eka idab amaammʌm miin, ndin ami mmaakʌp iso ke isọñ.<verse eid="DAN 10:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="DAN 10:10" />Ubọk amantuuk miin anyʌñ anam ubọk ye edọñ mmi eñnyeñ. <verse eid="DAN 10:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="DAN 10:11" />Anye amaabo, “Dandiel, afo amenekke anem Abasi esịd, nekke tịm kere baña mme ikọ a-ami mbooho udọkkọ fiin, nyʌñ dakka da, sia endọñ miin utom unọ fiin idahami.” Ndin ke anye amaaketañ ami annọ miin, ami mmaadakka nda ye ñnyeñidem.<verse eid="DAN 10:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="DAN 10:12" />Akem anye amaakaa iso, “Dandiel, kuufeghe ndịk. Tọọñọ ke akpa usen a-afo akebiideke ke akikere esịd mfo adibeeñe ifiọk ñnyʌñ nsuuho idem mfo ke iso Abasi mfo, emaekop akam uyio mfo, ndin ami ndi ke ibọọrọ ado. <verse eid="DAN 10:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="DAN 10:13" />Ado akpanabọọñ abio Pesia amambiọñọ miin ke usen edịb mme keed. Do ndin Maikel, keed ke atu mme enyere ukpeme abọọñ, amaadinnyaaña miin, sia ami ñkeba do ye adidem Pesia. <verse eid="DAN 10:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="DAN 10:14" />Idahami ami mmedi adinam nọ unwaña fiin se idiitịppe inọ mbon mfo ke iniiso, sia ñkukịd ado abaña ini se idiidi ke iso.”<verse eid="DAN 10:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="DAN 10:15" />Idaha a-anye aketañña ikọ ado ye ami, ami mmaasuuk iso mmi nse isọñ, ñkinyʌññọ ñkan nsio uyio. <verse eid="DAN 10:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="DAN 10:16" />Akem awo keed a-akebitte awodeen amaatuuk ñkpọkinua mmi, ndin ami mmaakʌppọ inua mmi ñnyʌñ ntọọñọ aditañ ikọ. Ami mmaabo anye a-akedaaha ke iso mmi nte, “Abọọñ mmi, ukuud añkan miin ubọk ato ke ntak ñkukịd ado, ñko idem ammem ataa eti-eti. <verse eid="DAN 10:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="DAN 10:17" />Abọọñ mmi, ami awo mfo, ñkeme die aditañ ikọ ye afo? Adudu mmi akweeñe, ñko a-anekke asọñ ami adinweek inweek.”<verse eid="DAN 10:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="DAN 10:18" />Ndin anye a-akebitte awo amaamaana antuuk miin anyʌñ annọ miin adudu. <verse eid="DAN 10:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="DAN 10:19" />Anye amaabo miin, “Kuuyak idem unyeñ, afo a-anekkeke anem Abasi esịd. Bọ emem! Sọñ idem idahami; sọñ idem.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="DAN 10:19">Idaha a-anye aketañña ikọ ye ami, ami mmaakop adudu ñnyʌñ mbo nte, “Abọọñ mmi tañ, sia afo amennọ miin adudu.”<verse eid="DAN 10:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="DAN 10:20" />Ndin enyere amaabo ate, “Afo amediọọñọ ntak a-ami ndiighe ubịne fiin? Ke etək ini ami ñyaatịmme ñkenwana ye akpanabọọñ Pesia, ndin ami mmaaka, akpanabọọñ Kriis ñko ayaadi; <verse eid="DAN 10:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="DAN 10:21" />ado ke akpa ifed ana ami udọkkọ fiin se ewet esịn ke Ñwed Akpanikọ. (Ibaaha awo se ida ye ami inwana ye ammọ ke amaaboiyo Maikel, akpanabọọñ mfo.<verse eid="DAN 10:21" /></para>
  <chapter eid="DAN 10" />
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="DAN 11" />
  <para style="nb">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="DAN 11:1" />Ñko ke akpa isua ukara Dariọs awo Miid, ami mmaawuọ nda adinwam ñnyʌñ ñkpeme anye).<verse eid="DAN 11:1" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ndidem Usuuk ye Adoro</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="DAN 11:2" />“Ami udọkkọ fiin akpanikọ: Ndidem ita mfen eyaedakka eda ukara ke Pesia, ndin ayọhọ inaañ ayaamọinyọ akan afịd mbon ñko. Anye amaabọ ukara akeene naña anye amọinyọ, anye ayaanam afịd mme awo eda keed etịppe ekọñ ye abio Kriis. <verse eid="DAN 11:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="DAN 11:3" />Ndin akpọsọñ adidem ayaadakka ada, anye adiikara ye akpọsọñ adudu anyʌñ anam se inemme anye. <verse eid="DAN 11:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="DAN 11:4" />Ke anye amaadakka ada ukara, eyaebakka abioubọọñ amọ enyʌñ edeeme anye edọñ ke ikpeghe afịm mbeñ anyọñ inaañ. Ukara ado idiikaaha ibịne mbon ubon amọ, idiinyʌññọ inie utọ adudu a-anye akenieghe, sia eyaedịppe ubọọñ amọ enọ mbon mfen.<verse eid="DAN 11:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="DAN 11:5" />“Adidem Usuuk ayaasọñ adudu, ado keed ke atu mme adaiso ekọñ amọ ayaasọñ adudu akan anye anyʌñ akara abioubọọñ amọ ye akpọsọñ adudu. <verse eid="DAN 11:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="DAN 11:6" />Ke mme isua ifañ emaeboiyo, ammọ eyaenam edioomo ndukoppo. Ayịn awonwaan adidem Usuuk ayaakaa ukañ adidem Adoro adinam emem ndukoppo, ado anye idiimʌmmọ adudu ke ifịm ubọọñ amọ ikama, ñko anye ye ubọọñ amọ idiikpeeneke. Ke mme usen ado, eyaebiaña anye ye afịd mme nsaña ubọọñ amọ ye ete amọ ye awo a-akedaaha ye anye.<verse eid="DAN 11:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="DAN 11:7" />“Awo keed a-atooho aduuk amọ ayaadakka ada adat itie amọ. Anye ayaanwana ye udịmekọñ adidem Adoro anyʌñ aboiyo adʌk akpọsọñ itie amọ, anye ayaanwana ye ammọ anyʌñ akan. <verse eid="DAN 11:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="DAN 11:8" />Anye ayaakoono mme abasi ammọ, mme usọsọi ñkpọ, mme ubobodñkpọ ukwak ammọ ye mme nsọñudua ñkpọ mme silfa ye kold ammọ anyʌñ atañ ammọ akaa ke Iyib. Ke ñkpọ nte isua ifañ anye ayaadakka akpọñ adidem Adoro. <verse eid="DAN 11:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="DAN 11:9" />Akem adidem Adoro ayaadi ekọñ ke isọñ ukara adidem Usuuk, ado anye ayaatịmme edem anyọñ abio amọ. <verse eid="DAN 11:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="DAN 11:10" />Nditọ amọ eyaebeeñe idem enọ ekọñ enyʌñ ekoot akwa atu mbon ekọñ ebon, e-ediikwọọk nte akaakan mmọọñ ukwọ enyʌñ enwana ekọñ tutu ekewuọ akpọsọñ itie adidem Usuuk.<verse eid="DAN 11:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="DAN 11:11" />“Ndin adidem Usuuk ayaasaña awuọ ke ikpakkaesịd ye udịmekọñ anyʌñ anwana ye adidem Adoro, a-adiikama akwa udịmekọñ, ado eyaekan anye. <verse eid="DAN 11:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="DAN 11:12" />Anye amaakan udịmekọñ ami, ntañidem ayaayọhọ adidem Usuuk idem ñko anye ayaawot uwak tọsịn, ado edikan amọ idiikpeeneke. <verse eid="DAN 11:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="DAN 11:13" />Sia adidem Adoro ayaamaana asio udịmekọñ mfen, a-awakka akan akpa; ndin ke uwak isua amaaboiyo, anye ayaatịmme adʌk ye ekamba udịmekọñ a-anieghe uwak ñkpọ ekọñ.<verse eid="DAN 11:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="DAN 11:14" />“Ke mme ini ado uwak awo eyaedakka eda utọk ye adidem Usuuk. Mbon afai ke atu mbon ndufo eyaenam ntịmme nọ ñkukịd ami asu, ado idiikịtte unen. <verse eid="DAN 11:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="DAN 11:15" />Ndin adidem Adoro ayaadibọp ikpọ ebono ekọñ anyʌñ amʌm akpọsọñ abio. Mbon ekọñ Usuuk idiikanna isọọñọ ida inwana ye ammọ; akpekọm ataa nti mbon ekọñ ammọ idiinieghe ukem adudu adinwana. <verse eid="DAN 11:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="DAN 11:16" />Andito ndi ekọñ ayaanam naña anye amama; awo ndomokeed idiikanna ida anye ke iso. Anye ayaasio idem amọ anịm ke Uyaiya Isọñ anyʌñ anie adudu adisobo anye. <verse eid="DAN 11:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="DAN 11:17" />Anye ayaabiide adiben adudu afịd abioubọọñ amọ ñnyʌñ nnam emem ndukoppo ye adidem Usuuk. Anye ñko ayaanọ adidem Usuuk adiaha amọ ke ndọ nọ ato do anye akan adooro anye ke ubọọñ, ado uduak amọ idiiwuọhọ isu, idiinwamma, idiinyʌññọ ifọn ye anye. <verse eid="DAN 11:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="DAN 11:18" />Ndin anye ayaakanna iso ase mme mben inyañ anyʌñ akan uwak ammọ, ado adaiso ekọñ keed ayaatre afịd usọñanyen amọ anyʌñ amaana akappa asuenne ado anọ anye. <verse eid="DAN 11:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="DAN 11:19" />Ke ami amaaboiyo, anye ayaatịmme edem, akappa iso ase mme akpọsọñ itie ke isọñ abio amọ, ado ayaatuak ukod aduọ, tutu awo ikịtte anye aba.<verse eid="DAN 11:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="DAN 11:20" />“Awo andidad itie amọ ayaasio awo ubọ taks nọ ekama enam ndutʌm abioubọọñ. Ke isua ifañ ke iso, eyaesobo anye, ado idiidooho ke iyadesịd me ke ekọñ.<verse eid="DAN 11:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="DAN 11:21" />“Ekpo-ekpo awo keed e-ediinọọhọ ukpono ubọọñ ayaadat itie amọ. Anye ayaadat ukara ke ini mme andinie abio ebaaha ke ifuuro, anye adiikama ñkara ye nneminua ibọ ukara. <verse eid="DAN 11:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="DAN 11:22" />Ke ami amaaboiyo eyaekwọọk ekandịk udịmekọñ esio ke iso amọ; eyaesobo anye ye akpanabọọñ edioomo efep. <verse eid="DAN 11:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="DAN 11:23" />Ke anye amaanyịmme nọ edʌk edioomo ye anye ima, anye ayaanam ido nsu, ñko ayaakama etək udịm awo ifañ amaana abọ ukara. <verse eid="DAN 11:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="DAN 11:24" />Ke ini mme ikpeghe ukara se imọinyọ ikan emaeba ke ifuuro, anye ayaanam ekọñ ye ammọ anyʌñ anam se mme ete ye mme eteete amọ imiikikanna inam. Anye ayaadeeme mme mbịme, ñkpọ ñwo ye inie anọ ikọd amọ. Anye ayaanam ndịbe uduak abaña adidat mme ñkpọsọñ itie adidem, ado idiikpeeneke.<verse eid="DAN 11:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="DAN 11:25" />“Anye ayaakama akwa udịmekọñ amọ ye adudu ye uko anam mfịna ye adidem Usuuk. Adidem Usuuk ayaaben akwa akpọsọñ udịmekọñ anam ekọñ, ado idiikanna, ato ke ntak mme ndịbe uduak e-ekenamma ebaña anye. <verse eid="DAN 11:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="DAN 11:26" />Mbon e-ediaha ndidia eto ke udeeme ñkpọ ufọk adidem eyaenwana adisobo anye; eyaekwọọk udịmekọñ amọ efep, ñko uwak eyaekpañña ke iso ekọñ. <verse eid="DAN 11:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="DAN 11:27" />Ndidem iba ami, e-esịd ammọ esʌkkọ eyem unam ibak, eyaebono ke akpokoro keed enyʌñ esʌhọ nsu enọ idem ammọ, ado ufọn idiibaaha, sia utịd ana adi ke ini e-ekenịmme. <verse eid="DAN 11:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="DAN 11:28" />Adidem Adoro ayaatịmme anyọñ abio amọ ye uwak inie, ado esịd amọ adiisʌk iwọwʌhọ ke adibiat adisana edioomo. Anye ayaanam uduak amọ ke abaña ado mbemiso anye atịmme anyọñ abio amọ.<verse eid="DAN 11:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="DAN 11:29" />“Ke akemini anye ayaamaana anam ekọñ ye Usuuk, ado isañ anyem idiidooho naña akedo akpa. <verse eid="DAN 11:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="DAN 11:30" />Mme nsʌñikañ e-etooho mme mben mmọọñ usobutịn eyaenwana ye anye, ndin esịd ayaabʌññọ anye. Ndin anye ayaatịmme edem akenwañña ifiobesịd amọ afʌk adisana edioomo. Anye ayaatịmme anyọñ akappa akewọt mbon se ikikanna edem iwọt adisana edioomo mfọn.<verse eid="DAN 11:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="DAN 11:31" />“Mme udịmekọñ amọ eyaedakka eda adisappa akpọsọñ itie tembịd eyaenyʌñ etre mme uwa esinamma afịd usen. Akem ammọ eyaesio mbubiam enịm a-adatta ñwuudo adi. <verse eid="DAN 11:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="DAN 11:32" />Anye ayaakama nneminua abiat mbon se ikisappa edioomo ado, ado mbon e-ediọọñọke Abasi ammọ eyaesọñ eda esịn anye.<verse eid="DAN 11:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="DAN 11:33" />“Mbon aniọñ eyaenọ uwak awo item, ado ke etək ini ammọ eyaekpañña ke akañkañ, imiidooho eyaefọp ubaak ke ikañ, emuum usʌk enyọñọ enyʌñ ebịme inie ubaak ammọ. <verse eid="DAN 11:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="DAN 11:34" />Ammọ emaeduọññọ, eyaebọ etək unwam, ndin mbon se idiinamma akpanikọ eyaekeene ammọ ke mbubịk. <verse eid="DAN 11:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="DAN 11:35" />Usʌk mbon aniọñ eyaetuak ukod, nọ ato do esịññe ammọ ndek ke idem, enam ammọ esana, enyʌñ enana ndo tutu utịd ini, sia ami ana atịppe ke ini e-ekenịmme.<verse eid="DAN 11:35" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adidem a-Akokkoke Idem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="DAN 11:36" />“Adidem ado adiinam se inem anye esịd. Anye ayaakokko idem anyʌñ anịm idem amọ nte ñkponñkan afịd ntək abasi, ayaanyʌñ atañ mme ñkpọ se awo idiikoppo akpa abaña Abasi mme abasi. Anye ayaakịt unen tutu ini ifiobesịd adikem, sia se ekebiere ana adat itie. <verse eid="DAN 11:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="DAN 11:37" />Anye idiidiọọñọke mme abasi mme eteete amọ me inọ anye se ibaan eyem, me ake abasi ndomokeed, ado ayaakokko idem amọ akan afịd ammọ. <verse eid="DAN 11:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="DAN 11:38" />Utu ke ado, anye ayaakpono abasi mme ñkpọsọñ itie, anye ayaakpono abasi a-mme eteete amọ imiikidiọọñọke ke kold ye silfa, ye nsọñudua itiad ye mme enọ. <verse eid="DAN 11:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="DAN 11:39" />Anye ayaanwana ye mme ñkponñkan akpọsọñ itie akeene unwam isen abasi, ndin ayaanyʌñ anekke akpono mbon se idiọọñọ anye. Anye ayaanam ammọ edo mme andikara uwak awo anyʌñ adeeme isọñ anọ ammọ ke ekọmudua.<verse eid="DAN 11:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="DAN 11:40" />“Ke ukpere edem ini adidem Usuuk ayaanwana ye anye ke iso ekọñ, ñko adidem Adoro ayaabịmme awuọ ye mme sariọd ye mbon ekọñ usaña ke enañmbakara ye akwa udịm ubom nsʌñikañ amọ. Anye ayaanam ekọñ ye uwak idʌñ anyʌñ akwọọk ammọ nte mmọọñ ukwọ. <verse eid="DAN 11:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="DAN 11:41" />Anye ayaakaa ekọñ ye Uyaiya Abio. Uwak mme abio eyaeduọññọ, ado Edọm, Mọb ye mme adaaha ke Amọn eyaebọkkọ. <verse eid="DAN 11:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="DAN 11:42" />Anye ayaatat ubọk adudu ukara amọ awuọ uwak idʌñ, Iyib ñko idiibọkkọke. <verse eid="DAN 11:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="DAN 11:43" />Anye ayaabọ mme itie unịm inie kold ye silfa ye afịd mme inie Iyib, ndin mbon Libia ye mbon Kuus eyaesuuk iwuod enọ anye. <verse eid="DAN 11:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="DAN 11:44" />Ado mme etob se idiito usakkautịn ye adoro eyaesịn anye ndịk ke idem, anye ñko ayaadakka ada ke akwa ikpakkaesịd adisobo ñnyʌñ ñwot uwak awo. <verse eid="DAN 11:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="DAN 11:45" />Anye ayaawuuk atayad ubọọñ amọ ke ufañ inyañ iba ke uyaiya adisana abod. Kpayeado, utịd amọ ayaadi, ndin awo ndomokeed idiinyaañake anye.<verse eid="DAN 11:45" /></para>
  <chapter eid="DAN 11" />
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="DAN 12" />
  <para style="s1">Mme Utịd Ini</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="DAN 12:1" />“Ke ini ado Maikel, akwa akpanabọọñ a-akpemeke mbon mfo, ayaadakka ada. Ini ukuud ayaaba a-adooho utọ ado ibaaha akpa tọọñọ ke ntọọñọ mme idịd tutu idaha ado. Ado ke ini ado ikọd mfo, afịd awo e-ekịtte ke emaewet anyịñ ke ñwed eyaebọkkọ. <verse eid="DAN 12:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="DAN 12:2" />Ataa uwak mme awo ekedaiyake ke ntọñ isọñ eyaedemme: ubaak ekaa uwem nsi-nsi, ubaak ebọ abuud ye nsi-nsi ndọk. <verse eid="DAN 12:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="DAN 12:3" />Mbon aniọñ eyaeyamma nte unwana anyọñ ye mbon se idat mme awo usʌñ ika adinenido, nte ntantaafiọñ ke nsi-nsi nsi-nsi. <verse eid="DAN 12:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="DAN 12:4" />Ado amaado afo, Dandiel, fʌk nyʌñ dịp mme ikọ ikpañwed ami tutu akpatre ini. Uwak awo eyaekaa umi ye uko edutịn adinam ifiọk ammọ atọt.”<verse eid="DAN 12:4" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="DAN 12:5" />Ndin Ami, Dandiel mmaase, ndin se awo iba mfen naña eda ke iso mmi, keed ke mbeñ inyañ umi, keed ke nsakiso uko. <verse eid="DAN 12:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="DAN 12:6" />Keed ke atu ammọ amaabịp awo a-akesịneke afọñ linen, a-akedoroke ke anyọñ mmọọñ inyañ ate, “Adiikpeene die mbemiso mme ñkpọ ñkpaidem ami ediwuọ esu?”<verse eid="DAN 12:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="DAN 12:7" />Awo a-akesịneke afọñ linen, a-akedoroke ke anyọñ mmọọñ inyañ, amaadịppe ubọk nnasia ye ubọk ufiin amọ ke mme hefịn, ndin ami mmaakop naña anye anwọñọ ke anye aduuho uwem ke nsi-nsi, ate, “Adiido ke ini, mme ini ye mbakka iba ini. Ke ini ediibiat adudu ndisana ikọd Abasi ke akpatre, eyaeben afịd mme ñkpọ ami ekesịm utịd.”<verse eid="DAN 12:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="DAN 12:8" />Ami mmaakop, ado ikiñnwañake. Ndin ami mmaabịp mbo, “abọọñ mmi, nsoo idiido utịd afịd ñkpọ ami?”<verse eid="DAN 12:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="DAN 12:9" />Anye amaabọọrọ, “Dandiel, kaa ndubeghe mfo, sia emaefʌk mme ikọ ami enyʌñ edịp ammọ tutu asịm akpatre ini. <verse eid="DAN 12:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="DAN 12:10" />Eyaesịññe uwak awo ndek ke idem, enam nọ enana ndo enyʌñ esana, ado mbon ibak eyaekaa iso ebak ibak. Ibaaha mbon ibak se idiidiọọñọ, ado mbon aniọñ eyaediọọñọ.<verse eid="DAN 12:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="DAN 12:11" />“Adiido usen tọsịn keed mme ikie iba mme anaañ mme duob tọọñọ ke ini se etre uwa afịd usen ye adisio mbubiam nnịm a-adiidat ñwuudo idi. <verse eid="DAN 12:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="DAN 12:12" />Afọfọn anọ awo a-abette tutu asịm utịd usen tọsịn keed mme ikie ita mme edịb mme duob mme ition.<verse eid="DAN 12:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="DAN 12:13" />“Amaado afo, kaa ndubeghe mfo tutu utịd adi. Afo ayaaduọk adudu, ndin ke mme akpatre usen afo ayaabọ udeeme e-ekenịmme unọọ fiin.”<verse eid="DAN 12:13" /></para>
  <chapter eid="DAN 12" />
</usx>